window.GLOWSIS_1B = [{"id": 9, "title": "I can't swim", "en": "저는 수영을 못 해요", "theme": "abilities", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 9 · ABILITIES</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">9</div><div><h2>I can't swim</h2><div class=\"en\">저는 수영을 못 해요 — Abilities · 못 + verb vs -(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · NEW SEASON · ABILITIES</span>\n      <h3>재능을 보여 줘요 — \"뭐를 할 수 있어요?\"</h3>\n      <p>예능 방송에서 다섯 멤버가 <b>재능</b>을 보여 줘요. <b>유나</b>는 춤추고, <b>서연</b>은 노래하고... 그런데 <b>운전</b>은 아무도 못 해요! \"아이돌처럼 노래하고 춤출 수 있어요. 하지만 운전은 못 해요!\" 😂</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">On a variety show, the five members show off their <b>talents</b>. <b>Yuna</b> dances, <b>Seoyeon</b> sings… but nobody can <b>drive</b>! \"I can sing and dance like an idol. But I can't drive!\" 😂</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">✨ NEW POINT · Talk about what you can &amp; can't do!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Say what you can &amp; can't do</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💪</span> 못 + verb (can't) vs -(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 (can)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎨</span> Hobby &amp; ability vocabulary</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 9 — Talent Check</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎪 Idol variety show</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-01.webp\" alt=\"지우\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지우</div><div class=\"ko\">여러분, 뭐를 할 수 있어요? 저는 노래를 부를 수 있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Everyone, what can you do? I can sing!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-05.webp\" alt=\"유나\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">유나</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 수영을 할 수 있어요! 그리고 춤도 출 수 있어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I can swim! And I can dance too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-01.webp\" alt=\"지훈\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">지훈</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 자전거를 탈 수 있어요. 운동을 좋아해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I can ride a bike. I like exercising!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/m-05.webp\" alt=\"하준\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">하준</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 피아노를 칠 수 있어요. 그런데 수영은 못 해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I can play the piano. But I can't swim.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/img/chars/f-02.webp\" alt=\"서연\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">서연</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 다섯 명 모두 뭔가를 잘 해요! 운전은 못 하지만요! 😂</div><div class=\"gl\">All five of us are good at something — even if we can't drive! 😂</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어요 — Everyday present tense (I do…)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say what you <b>do</b> in friendly polite speech, add <b>-아요/-어요</b> to the verb stem. Nouns that take <b>하다</b> (do) become <b>해요</b>: 운동하다 → 운동을 해요.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 매일 운동을 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I exercise every day. (하다 → 해요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">유나는 달리기를 좋아해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Yuna likes running.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서연은 노래를 불러요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Seoyeon sings. (부르다 → 불러요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">못 + verb — \"can't\" (no ability)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>못</b> right before a verb to say you <b>can't</b> do it because you don't have the skill. It's short and very common: <b>못 해요</b> = \"can't do\". (Not \"don't want to\" — that's different!)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 수영을 못 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't swim.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하준은 자전거를 못 타요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Hajun can't ride a bike.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 운전을 못 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't drive.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 — \"can\" (ability)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">To say you <b>can</b> do something, add <b>-ㄹ 수 있어요</b> after a vowel and <b>-을 수 있어요</b> after a final consonant. So 못 (can't) and ㄹ 수 있어요 (can) are the two sides of ability!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 수영할 수 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can swim. (수영하다 → 수영할 수 있어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">피아노를 칠 수 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can play the piano. (치다 → 칠 수 있어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지훈은 일본어를 읽을 수 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Jihoon can read Japanese. (받침 ㄱ → 을 수 있어요)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저는 수영을 못 해요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 수영을 못 해요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I can't swim.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How do Korean idols say \"I <b>can</b> sing\" and \"I <b>can't</b> swim\"? Two handy patterns live at the end of the verb.</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English we have a separate word \"can\". Korean instead uses endings glued onto the verb: <b>못 + verb</b> for \"can't\"\n      (no skill) and <b>-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</b> for \"can\". Today's model sentence uses <b>못 해요</b> = \"can't do\":\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">수영을 못 해요</span> = \"can't swim\". To flip it to \"can\", drop 못 and add ㄹ 수 있어요:\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">수영할 수 있어요</span> = \"can swim\". One idea, two tiny endings!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저는</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">as for me <span class=\"t-sub\">(topic)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = humble \"I\". Add the topic marker <b>는</b> to introduce who you're talking about.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">수영을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">swimming <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">수영 is the activity. <b>을</b> marks it as the object of the verb \"do\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">못 해요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">can't do <span class=\"t-sub\">(못 + 해요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\"><b>못</b> + <b>해요</b> (present of 하다/do) = \"can't do\". Change to <b>할 수 있어요</b> for \"can do\".</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">못 + verb = \"can't\"</b> — put 못 right before the verb to say you lack the ability. <b>수영을 못 해요</b> = \"I can't swim\",\n    <b>운전을 못 해요</b> = \"I can't drive\". Remember 못 talks about <b>ability</b> — not being forbidden or not wanting to.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>못 + verb → can't (no ability)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 수영을 못 해요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I can't swim.\" — I don't have the skill.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 → can (have ability)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">저는 수영할 수 있어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I can swim.\" — I have the ability.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> ability has two doors — <b>못 + verb</b> (can't) and <b>-ㄹ/을 수 있어요</b> (can). Ask a friend:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">뭐를 할 수 있어요?</span> (\"What can you do?\") and answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">○○을 할 수 있어요!</span> Like an idol on stage!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏃</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">운동과 활동<small>Exercise & activities · 뭐를 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_exercise.webp\" alt=\"운동\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운동')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">운동</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">undong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">exercise</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_swim.webp\" alt=\"수영\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('수영')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">수영</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">suyeong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">swimming</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_run.webp\" alt=\"달리기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('달리기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">달리기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dalligi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">running</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_bike.webp\" alt=\"자전거\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('자전거')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">자전거</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jajeongeo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bicycle</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 매일 운동을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 매일 운동을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I exercise every day.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('유나는 수영을 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">유나는 수영을 할 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Yuna can swim.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 달리기를 좋아해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 달리기를 좋아해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like running.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('하준은 자전거를 탈 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">하준은 자전거를 탈 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hajun can ride a bike.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏃 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 활동 + 을/를 + verb. 운동<b>을</b> 해요 (do exercise), 수영<b>을</b> 해요, 달리기<b>를</b> 해요, 자전거<b>를</b> 타요. Add 못 before the verb to say you can't.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎨</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">취미<small>Hobbies · 그림과 요리</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_paint.webp\" alt=\"그림\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('그림')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">그림</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geurim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">drawing / picture</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_cook.webp\" alt=\"요리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">요리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cooking</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 그림을 그려요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 그림을 그려요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I draw pictures.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 그림을 그릴 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 그림을 그릴 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can draw.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서연은 요리를 잘 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">서연은 요리를 잘 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Seoyeon cooks well.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 요리를 못 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 요리를 못 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can't cook.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎨 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 그림<b>을</b> 그려요 (draw), 요리<b>를</b> 해요 (cook). 그리다 → 그릴 수 있어요, 하다 → 할 수 있어요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎹</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">배우는 것<small>Skills to learn · 오래 연습해요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_comp.webp\" alt=\"컴퓨터\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('컴퓨터')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">컴퓨터</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">keomyuteo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">computer</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b9_piano.webp\" alt=\"피아노\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('피아노')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">피아노</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">piano</div><div class=\"vw-en\">piano</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지훈은 컴퓨터를 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지훈은 컴퓨터를 할 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Jihoon can use a computer.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 컴퓨터를 못 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 컴퓨터를 못 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can't use a computer.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('하준은 피아노를 칠 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">하준은 피아노를 칠 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hajun can play the piano.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 피아노를 못 쳐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 피아노를 못 쳐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can't play the piano.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎹 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 컴퓨터<b>를</b> 해요 (use a computer), 피아노<b>를</b> 쳐요 (play piano). Piano and computer take hours of practice — 치다 → 칠 수 있어요!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-1] Reading — 저는 수영을 못 해요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우: 저는 수영을 못 해요.</span> What does Jiwoo say?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I can swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I can't swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I swim every day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I want to swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The word <b class=\"hl\">못</b> before a verb = <b class=\"hl\">\"can't\"</b>. <b>수영을 못 해요</b> means <span class=\"pt-ko\">수영</span>(swimming) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 해요</span>(can't do) = \"I can't swim\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">I can swim</b> would be 수영<b class=\"hl\">할 수 있어요</b> (ㄹ 수 있어요 = can); the other two add ideas (every day / want) not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: ability \"can't\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 + verb</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-2] Reading — 수영할 수 있어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">유나: 저는 수영할 수 있어요.</span> What does Yuna mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I can't swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I will swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I can swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q2',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I like swimming.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The ending <b class=\"hl\">-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</b> = <b class=\"hl\">\"can\"</b> (ability). <b>수영하다 → 수영할 수 있어요</b> = \"I can swim\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">can't</b> would use 못 (수영을 못 해요); the others say future or liking, not ability.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: ability \"can\" → <span class=\"pt-ko\">verb + ㄹ/을 수 있어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-3] Reading — 운동을 해요 (-아/어요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite present tense.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 매일 운동을 (　).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 해요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 해<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 할 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <b class=\"hl\">하다</b> (do) becomes <b class=\"hl\">해요</b> in the friendly present tense. With an activity noun you say <span class=\"pt-ko\">운동을 해요</span> = \"I do exercise / I exercise\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">해</b> is not polite, <b class=\"hl\">했어요</b> is the past, and <b class=\"hl\">할 거예요</b> is the future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 하다 → 해요 (present). Nouns like 운동·요리·수영 take 을/를 + 해요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-4] Reading — 자전거를 못 타요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence means \"Hajun can't ride a bike\"?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the sentence with the meaning \"can't do it\".</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 하준은 자전거를 탈 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 하준은 자전거를 타요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 하준은 자전거를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q4',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 하준은 자전거를 못 타요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To say <b class=\"hl\">\"can't ride a bike\"</b> use <b class=\"hl\">못</b> before the verb: <span class=\"pt-ko\">자전거를 못 타요</span> = \"can't ride a bike\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">탈 수 있어요</b> means CAN ride, <b class=\"hl\">타요</b> just means rides, and <b class=\"hl\">좋아해요</b> means likes.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 못 + 타요 = can't ride. After ㄹ the \"can\" form is <span class=\"pt-ko\">탈 수 있어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-5] Listening — what can't he do?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker CANNOT do.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('하준은 운전을 못 해요. 하지만 자전거를 탈 수 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What can't the speaker do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 운전하기 (driving)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 자전거 타기 (riding a bike)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 수영하기 (swimming)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 그림 그리기 (drawing)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">하준은 운전을 못 해요</span> = \"Hajun can't drive\". The <b class=\"hl\">못 해요</b> answers \"can't\" = <b class=\"hl\">driving</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The rider continues <span class=\"pt-ko\">자전거를 탈 수 있어요</span> = he CAN ride a bike, so bike is the wrong answer.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 해요</span> (can't) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">할 수 있어요</span> (can).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-6] Reading — 그림을 그릴 수 있어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서연: 저는 그림을 그릴 수 있어요.</span> What can Seoyeon do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She can cook.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She can draw.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She can't draw.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She can swim.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">그림을 그릴 수 있어요</span> = \"can draw pictures\". <b>그리다 → 그릴 수 있어요</b> is the ability form of \"to draw\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Cooking is 요리, swimming is 수영, and \"can't draw\" would use 못 — none match 그릴 수 있어요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 그리다 ends in the vowel ㅣ, so we add <span class=\"pt-ko\">-ㄹ 수 있어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-7] Reading — choose the wrong sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is NOT correct?</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Pick the sentence that has a mistake.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 요리를 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 피아노를 칠 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 수영을 못 할 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q7',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 운동을 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You can't stack <b class=\"hl\">못</b> and <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ 수 있어요</b> together — <b>못 할 수 있어요</b> is wrong. Use one or the other: <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 해요</span> (can't) or <span class=\"pt-ko\">할 수 있어요</span> (can).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">요리를 못 해요</b> (can't cook), <b class=\"hl\">피아노를 칠 수 있어요</b> (can play piano), and <b class=\"hl\">운동을 해요</b> (I exercise) are all correct sentences.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 못 and ㄹ 수 있어요 both express ability — never combine them.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-8] Listening — who can swim?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose who CAN swim.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지훈은 수영을 못 해요. 그런데 유나는 수영을 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Listen to the audio. Who can swim?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지훈<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 유나<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 서연<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 하준<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">지훈은 수영을 못 해요</span> (Jihoon can't swim), but <span class=\"pt-ko\">유나는 수영을 할 수 있어요</span> (Yuna CAN swim). The ability speaker is <b class=\"hl\">유나</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Jihoon has 못 (can't), and the other two names are not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 못 → can't, ㄹ 수 있어요 → can. Who has the ability?</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-9] Reading — what CAN you do?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best reply to the question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">뭐를 할 수 있어요?</span> (What can you do?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 운전을 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 커피를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저는 달리기를 할 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 지금 바빠요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question asks <b class=\"hl\">\"What can you do?\"</b>, so the answer needs the <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ 수 있어요</b> ability form. <b>달리기를 할 수 있어요</b> = \"I can run\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others talk about driving (못 = can't), coffee (liking), and being busy — none answer \"can do what\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer ability questions with <span class=\"pt-ko\">○○할 수 있어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9-10] Listening — the idol summary</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 노래를 할 수 있고 춤도 출 수 있어요. 하지만 운전은 못 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker say about herself?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u9q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> She can sing and dance.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> She can't sing or dance.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> She can drive.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u9q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> She can only dance.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u9q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">노래를 할 수 있고 춤도 출 수 있어요</span> (I can sing and also dance) — so the best summary is <b class=\"hl\">she can sing and dance</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">She ends with <span class=\"pt-ko\">하지만 운전은 못 해요</span> (but I can't drive), so driving is wrong, and she does NOT say she can't sing or dance.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Like an idol — can sing + can dance + can't drive. Listen for <span class=\"pt-ko\">-ㄹ 수 있어요</span> (can) and <span class=\"pt-ko\">못</span> (can't).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Sing Like a K-POP Idol!</h3>\n    <p>On every stage idols prove what they can do. But even idols can't do everything — that's what practice is for! Say what YOU can do, and what you can't.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"저는 ○○할 수 있어요. ○○은 못 해요. 하지만 연습하면 할 수 있어요!\" — \"(I can ○○. I can't ○○. But with practice, I can!)\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 10, "title": "Shall we have lunch?", "en": "같이 점심을 먹을까요?", "theme": "suggestions", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 10 · SUGGESTIONS</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">10</div><div><h2>Shall we have lunch?</h2><div class=\"en\">같이 점심을 먹을까요? — Making suggestions · 함께</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 함께</span>\n      <h3>아란의 제안 — \"같이 먹을까요?\"</h3>\n      <p>리더 <b>아란</b>은 데뷔 준비를 마치고 멤버들에게 <b>함께 하자</b>고 제안해요. \"같이 점심을 먹을까요?\" — 함께 하는 시간이 가장 행복해요. 💛</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Leader <b>Aran</b> finishes practice and makes <b>suggestions</b> to the members. \"같이 점심을 먹을까요?\" (Shall we have lunch together?) — time spent together is the happiest. 💛</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 10/10 획득 — Making suggestions!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Make a suggestion with -ㄹ까요?</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤝</span> 같이/함께 \"together\"</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🍚</span> Meals, drinks & activities vocabulary</div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 10 — After Practice</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📺 Practice room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">연습 끝났어요! 같이 점심을 먹을까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Practice is done! Shall we have lunch together?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 같이 밥을 먹어요. 그런데 뭐 먹을까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Sounds good! Let's eat together. But what shall we eat?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">커피 마실까요? 아니면 차를 마실까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Shall we have coffee? Or shall we have tea?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">배고파요. 빨리 먹어요! 그리고 저녁에 같이 영화를 볼까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm hungry. Let's eat fast! And shall we watch a movie together tonight?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 같이 노래방에도 갈까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! Shall we go to the noraebang (karaoke) together too?</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ까요? — \"Shall we ~?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Make a <b>suggestion</b> by adding <b>-(으)ㄹ까요?</b> to a verb stem. After a vowel use <b>-ㄹ까요?</b>, after a final consonant use <b>-을까요?</b>. It feels like \"Shall we…?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 점심을 먹<b>을까요</b>?</span><span class=\"gl\">먹다 has the final consonant ㄱ → 을까요</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 영화를 보<b>ㄹ까요</b>?</span><span class=\"gl\">보다 ends in the vowel ㅗ → ㄹ까요</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 노래방에 갈까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we go to the noraebang together?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">같이 / 함께 — \"together\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Both mean <b>together</b>. <b>같이</b> is everyday spoken, <b>함께</b> is a little more formal or literary. Put it right before the verb.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>같이</b> 먹을까요?</span><span class=\"gl\">Shall we eat together?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>함께</b> 노래해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Let's sing together.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">친구와 <b>같이</b> 영화를 봐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I watch movies together with my friend.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어요 — casual polite suggestion</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The everyday polite ending <b>-아요/-어요</b> can also make a gentle suggestion: \"Let's ~\". After 아/오 vowels use <b>-아요</b>, otherwise <b>-어요</b>. Great for agreeing with a friend's idea!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 가<b>요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">가다 ends in ㅏ → 가요 · Let's go together.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">커피 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">마시다 → 마셔요 · Let's have coffee.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 먹<b>어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">먹다 → 먹어요 · Let's eat together.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"같이 점심을 먹을까요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">같이 점심을 먹을까요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Shall we have lunch together?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why do idols keep asking <b>…ㄹ까요?</b> instead of just saying what to do?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      A question ending in <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> turns a verb into a friendly <b>proposal</b>. English says \"Shall we…? / Should we…?\"\n      Korean puts it on the very end of the sentence. <b>먹다</b> (to eat) becomes <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹을까요?</span> — \"shall (we) eat?\"\n      The whole sentence: <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이</span> (together) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">점심을</span> (lunch-object) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹을까요?</span> (shall eat?). Ask first, act together — that's Korean friendliness!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">같이</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">together <span class=\"t-sub\">(adverb)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Sits before the verb to say \"together\". <b>함께</b> is its slightly more formal twin.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">점심<b>을</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">lunch <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">점심 has the final consonant ㅁ → object particle <b>을</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹<b>을까요?</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">shall (we) eat? <span class=\"t-sub\">(suggestion)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">먹다 stem 먹 has 받침 ㄱ → <b>-을까요?</b>. A vowel would give <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> (보다 → 볼까요?).</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄹ까요? = \"Shall we…?\"</b> — attach it to a verb stem and the whole sentence becomes a soft proposal.\n    Pick <b>-을까요?</b> after a consonant (먹<b>을까요</b>) and <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> after a vowel (보<b>ㄹ까요</b>, 가<b>ㄹ까요</b>).\n    Answer <span class=\"pt-ko\">좋아요!</span> (good!) to say yes, or <span class=\"pt-ko\">싫어요</span> to say no.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Final consonant (받침) → -을까요?</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">먹<b>다</b> → 먹<b>을까요?</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">받침 ㄱ → \"Shall (we) eat?\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Vowel → -ㄹ까요?</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">보<b>다</b> → 보<b>ㄹ까요?</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">No 받침 → \"Shall (we) watch?\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> the suggestion ending <b>-ㄹ까요?</b> works like a question mark you glue onto a verb.\n    <b>Consonant → 을까요?</b>, <b>vowel → ㄹ까요?</b> — the same 받침 idea from <span class=\"pt-ko\">은/는</span> and <span class=\"pt-ko\">이에요/예요</span>.\n    Combine it with <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이</span> for the classic K-POP group move: <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 노래방에 갈까요?</span> (Shall we go to the noraebang together?)\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍚</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">하루 세 끼<small>Meals · 언제 먹어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_breakfast.webp\" alt=\"아침\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아침</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">achim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">breakfast / morning</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_lunch.webp\" alt=\"점심\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('점심')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">점심</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeomsim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">lunch / noon</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_dinner.webp\" alt=\"저녁\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">저녁</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jeonyeok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dinner / evening</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아침에 뭐 먹어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아침에 뭐 먹어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What do you eat for breakfast?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 점심을 먹을까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 점심을 먹을까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we have lunch together?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저녁에 같이 영화를 볼까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저녁에 같이 영화를 볼까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we watch a movie together in the evening?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍚 <b>하루 세 끼:</b> 아침 → 점심 → 저녁 = breakfast → lunch → dinner. Say them with <b>같이 …을까요?</b> to invite a friend to any meal!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">☕</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">음료<small>Drinks · 무엇을 마셔요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_coffee.webp\" alt=\"커피\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('커피')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">커피</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">keopi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">coffee</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_tea.webp\" alt=\"차\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('차')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">차</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">cha</div><div class=\"vw-en\">tea</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('커피 마실까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">커피 마실까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we have some coffee?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아니면 차를 마실까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아니면 차를 마실까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Or shall we have some tea?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">☕ <b>커피 vs 차:</b> both take <b>마시다</b> (to drink): <span class=\"pt-ko\">커피를 마시다</span>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">차를 마시다</span>. 차 ends in ㅏ → <b>차를</b>.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎬</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">함께 즐기기<small>Doing things together · 같이</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_together.webp\" alt=\"같이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">같이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gachi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">together</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_movie.webp\" alt=\"영화\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('영화')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">영화</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeonghwa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">movie</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_walk.webp\" alt=\"산책\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('산책')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">산책</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sanchae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">walk / stroll</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 영화를 볼까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 영화를 볼까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we watch a movie together?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 산책할까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 산책할까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we take a walk together?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('함께 노래해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">함께 노래해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's sing together.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎬 <b>같이 + verb:</b> put <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이</span> (or <span class=\"pt-ko\">함께</span>) before the verb to share any activity — <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 영화를 봐요</span>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 산책해요</span>. Verb for 영화 = 보다 (watch), for 산책 = 산책하다 (take a walk).</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-1] Reading — 먹을까요 (받침 rule)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct suggestion ending.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">같이 점심을 (　)요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹을까요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 먹다 stem has 받침 ㄱ → 을까요?</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹까요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Can't drop the 을 syllable</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹을까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ The polite ? is needed</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹을까여<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not a real ending</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <span class='pt-ko'>먹다</span> (to eat) has the final consonant <b class='hl'>ㄱ</b> (받침), so the suggestion ending is <b class='hl'>-을까요?</b>: <span class='pt-ko'>먹을까요?</span> = \"shall (we) eat?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class='hl'>먹까요</b> drops the 을 syllable and is wrong.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: 받침(consonant) → <span class='pt-ko'>을까요?</span>; vowel → <span class='pt-ko'>ㄹ까요?</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-2] Reading — 볼까요 (vowel rule)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct suggestion ending.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">같이 영화를 (　)요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 보을까요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 보다 has no 받침</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 볼까요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 보다 ends in vowel ㅗ → ㄹ까요?</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 보까요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Need the ㄹ before 까요</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 봐까요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ That's the -아요 form, not a suggestion</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <span class='pt-ko'>보다</span> (to watch) has no 받침 (ends in vowel ㅗ), so it takes <b class='hl'>-ㄹ까요?</b>: <span class='pt-ko'>볼까요?</span> = \"shall (we) watch?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class='hl'>보을까요</b> wrongly adds 을 after a vowel.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class='pt-ko'>같이 영화를 볼까요?</span> — the classic movie-night invite!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-3] Reading — 같이 (together)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which word means \"together\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">다음 중 '함께'와 뜻이 같은 말을 고르세요. (Choose the word with the same meaning as 함께.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 혼자<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 혼자 = alone</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 같이<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 같이 and 함께 both mean together</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 조금<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 조금 = a little</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 자주<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 자주 = often</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class='hl'>함께</b> and <span class='pt-ko'>같이</span> both mean <b class='hl'>together</b> — 함께 is a touch more formal/literary.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class='hl'>혼자</b> (alone) is the opposite, <b class='hl'>조금</b> and <b class='hl'>자주</b> are different adverbs.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Pair them with a verb: <span class='pt-ko'>같이 먹어요</span> = \"let's eat together\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-4] Reading — 무엇을 제안해요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose what is suggested.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"같이 점심을 먹을까요?\" — 무슨 제안이에요? (What is being suggested?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 함께 저녁을 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ It says 점심 (lunch), not 저녁</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 혼자 영화를 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not alone, and not a movie</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 같이 점심을 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ The suggestion is to eat lunch together</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 같이 노래를 불러요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ No singing is mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question <span class='pt-ko'>같이 점심을 먹을까요?</span> = \"Shall we eat lunch <b class='hl'>together</b>?\" — it suggests eating lunch together.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options mention 저녁/영화/노래 (dinner/movie/singing), not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Key words: <span class='pt-ko'>같이</span> (together) and <span class='pt-ko'>점심</span> (lunch).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-5] Reading — 가요 (-아요 suggestion)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct -아/어요 ending.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">같이 (　)요. (Let's go together.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Need the polite 요 ending</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 가다 ends in ㅏ → 가요</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 가아요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Too long; 가다 only takes one 아</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 어요 is for other vowels</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class='pt-ko'>가다</span> (to go) ends in the vowel <b class='hl'>ㅏ</b>, so it takes <b class='hl'>-아요</b> → <span class='pt-ko'>가요</span>. This -아/어요 form makes a soft \"let's ~\" suggestion.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class='hl'>가아요 / 가어요</b> over-add endings.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 After ㅏ/ㅗ use <span class='pt-ko'>-아요</span>, after other vowels use <span class='pt-ko'>-어요</span>: <span class='pt-ko'>마셔요</span>, <span class='pt-ko'>먹어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-6] Reading — 점심 (meal vocab)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct word.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"저는 오후 12시에 밥을 먹어요.\" — 몇 시에 먹어요? (What meal time?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 아침<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 아침 = breakfast / morning</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 점심<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ Noon (12시) is lunch = 점심</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저녁<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 저녁 = dinner / evening</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 간식<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 간식 = snack</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence says <b class='hl'>오후 12시</b> (12 noon), which is lunchtime → <span class='pt-ko'>점심</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class='hl'>아침</b> is morning, <b class='hl'>저녁</b> is evening, <b class='hl'>간식</b> is a snack.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Meal times: 아침(morning) → 점심(noon) → 저녁(evening).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-7] Listening — 커피 마실까요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what drink is suggested.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('커피 마실까요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">커피 마실까요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 커피<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ You heard 커피 마실까요? = shall we have coffee?</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 차<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not tea</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 물<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not water</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 우유<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not milk</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio asks <span class='pt-ko'>커피 마실까요?</span> = \"Shall we have <b class='hl'>coffee</b>?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 차/물/우유 (tea/water/milk) were not mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class='pt-ko'>마시다</span> (to drink) + <span class='pt-ko'>-ㄹ까요?</span> → <span class='pt-ko'>마실까요?</span></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-8] Listening — 저녁에 먹어요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what meal time is mentioned.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저녁에 같이 먹어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">저녁에 같이 먹어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 아침<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not breakfast</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 점심<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not lunch</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저녁<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ You heard 저녁에 = in the evening/dinner</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 간식<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not a snack</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class='pt-ko'>저녁에 같이 먹어요</span> — the meal time is <b class='hl'>저녁</b> (dinner/evening).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 아침/점심/간식 (breakfast/lunch/snack) were not said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class='pt-ko'>저녁에</span> = \"in the evening\", with the time particle <b class='hl'>에</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-9] Listening — 영화를 볼까요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what is suggested.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('같이 영화를 볼까요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">같이 영화를 볼까요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 같이 음악을 들어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not music</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 혼자 영화를 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ It says 같이 (together)</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 같이 영화를 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ You heard 같이 영화를 볼까요? = watch a movie together</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 같이 노래를 불러요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not singing</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio asks <span class='pt-ko'>같이 영화를 볼까요?</span> = \"Shall we watch a <b class='hl'>movie together</b>?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others mention 음악/혼자/노래 (music/alone/singing), not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class='pt-ko'>같이 …볼까요?</span> is the go-to K-POP movie invite.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[[10-10] Listening — 차를 마실까요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what drink is suggested.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('차를 마실까요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">차를 마실까요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u10q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 커피<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not coffee</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 차<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ You heard 차를 마실까요? = shall we have tea?</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 주스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not juice</span></button>\n<button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u10q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 맥주<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not beer</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u10q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio asks <span class='pt-ko'>차를 마실까요?</span> = \"Shall we have <b class='hl'>tea</b>?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 커피/주스/맥주 (coffee/juice/beer) were not said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class='pt-ko'>차를</span> — 차 ends in ㅏ (vowel) → object particle <b class='hl'>를</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Suggestions Challenge!</h3>\n    <p>Idols are always making plans together after practice. Ask a friend to join you!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"같이 노래방에 갈까요?\" — Shall we go to the noraebang (K-pop karaoke) together? Invite someone with -ㄹ까요? and answer 좋아요! (Sounds good!)</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 11, "title": "It's spicy so I can't eat it", "en": "떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요", "theme": "reasons", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 11 · REASONS — 매워서 못 먹어요</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">11</div><div><h2>It's spicy so I can't eat it</h2><div class=\"en\">떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요 — Reasons with -아서/어서</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">🍜 GLOWSIS STORY · 11 — Eating Show</span>\n      <h3>글로시스 먹방 — \"떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘 글로시스는 인기 <b>먹방</b>(eating show)에 나갔어요. 매운 <b>떡볶이</b> 앞에서 다들 \"너무 매워서 못 먹어요!\" 하고 울었어요. 하지만 <b>로이</b>는 맵고 배고파서 정말 많이 먹었어요! 🌶️</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today Glowsis appeared on a popular <b>먹방</b> (eating show). Facing the spicy <b>떡볶이</b>, everyone cried \"It's too spicy so I can't eat it!\" But <b>Roy</b>, hungry and brave, ate a whole lot! 🌶️</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🍜 GLOW POINT 11 — Give a reason with -아서/어서!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🌶️</span> Give a reason: -아서/어서 (so…)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">😅</span> Say you can't well: 잘 못</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">➕</span> Link actions: -고 (and)</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 11 — Spicy Tteokbokki Challenge</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🍜 Eating show set</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">먹방 시작! 떡볶이는 정말 맛있어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Let's start the eating show! Tteokbokki is really delicious.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">그런데 떡볶이는 매워요. 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">But tteokbokki is spicy. It's so spicy I can't eat it well.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">맞아요. 눈도 오고 추워서 따뜻한 음식이 좋아요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Right. It's snowing and it's cold, so I like warm food.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 배고파서 고추도 먹고 떡볶이도 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I'm hungry, so I eat peppers AND tteokbokki!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">와, 로이! 매운 음식을 잘 먹어요. 정말 대단해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Wow, Roy! You eat spicy food well. You're amazing!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아서/어서 — \"because…, so…\" (reason)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Take an adjective/verb stem and add <b>아서</b> (stem vowel ㅏ/ㅗ) or <b>어서</b> (any other vowel) to give the REASON. It feels like \"so\" or \"that's why\": <b>매워서 못 먹어요</b> = it's spicy, so I can't eat it.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">떡볶이는 매워<b>서</b> 못 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Tteokbokki is spicy, SO I can't eat it.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">추워<b>서</b> 집에 있어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's cold, SO I stay home.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">피곤해<b>서</b> 일찍 자요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm tired, SO I sleep early.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">잘 못 — \"can't (do) well\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>잘</b> = \"well\". Put <b>못</b> before a verb to say \"can't\". Together <b>잘 못 + verb</b> = \"can't do it well\" — you try, but it's hard. K-POP idols say this about super-spicy food and hard dance moves!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">매운 음식을 <b>잘 못</b> 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't eat spicy food well.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저는 춤을 <b>잘 못</b> 춰요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't dance well.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국어를 <b>잘 못</b> 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't speak Korean well.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 — \"…and…\" (linking)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-고</b> to a verb stem to chain two actions or facts: \"I do A <b>and</b> do B\". It's the K-POP way to list everything you're doing at once!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">고추도 먹<b>고</b> 떡볶이도 먹어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I eat peppers AND tteokbokki.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">눈도 오<b>고</b> 추워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It's snowing AND it's cold.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래를 듣<b>고</b> 춤을 춰요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I listen to music AND dance.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Why \"매워서 못 먹어요\"?</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Tteokbokki is spicy, so I can't eat it well.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Korean never says \"because\" as its own little word at the START. How does it glue the reason onto the end instead?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English you say <b>\"Because it is spicy, I can't eat it\"</b> — the reason comes first. Korean does the SAME thing but marks the reason by changing the adjective's ending to\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아서/어서</span>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">매워<b>서</b></span> = \"[because it is] spicy\". There is no separate \"because\". The reason always comes <b>before</b> the result, glued to the first clause.\n      Then <span class=\"pt-ko\">잘 못 먹어요</span> = \"I can't eat it well\" (잘 well + 못 can't + 먹어요 eat).\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">매워<b>서</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">[because it is] spicy <span class=\"t-sub\">(reason)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">맵다 (spicy) → stem 매운... The ㅂ drops and becomes <b>매워서</b>. Stem vowel ㅘ? no, it's a ㅂ-irregular: 맵다 → <b>매워</b> + 서.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">잘 못</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">can't (do) well <span class=\"t-sub\">(ability)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">잘 = well, 못 = cannot. <b>잘 못 먹어요</b> = \"I can't eat well\" — not \"I never eat it\", just that it's hard.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹어요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I eat <span class=\"t-sub\">(verb)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">The result comes last: spicy, so <b>I can't eat it</b>. Reason first, result after.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-아서 vs -어서 = vowel harmony</b> — the ending matches the verb's stem vowel. Vowel ㅏ or ㅗ → <b>-아서</b> (아파서, 배고파서). Any other vowel → <b>-어서</b> (피곤해서, 재미있어서). And a ㅂ stem like 맵다/춥다 becomes <b>매워서 / 추워서</b>!\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>ㅏ/ㅗ vowel → -아서</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">배고파<b>서</b> 밥을 먹어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">배고프다 (hungry) → 배고파서 → \"I'm hungry so I eat.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Other vowel → -어서</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">피곤해<b>서</b> 자요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">피곤하다 (tired) → 피곤해서 → \"I'm tired so I sleep.\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아서/어서</span> as a green traffic light between reason and result — the reason makes the result happen. To turn it into a LIST instead of a reason, swap the ending for <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고</span>:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">고추도 먹<b>고</b> 떡볶이도 먹어요</span> (I eat peppers AND tteokbokki). Same first-clause spot, two different jobs!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🥵</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">이유를 말해요<small>Reason words · 왜 못 해요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">6</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_fever.webp\" alt=\"아파서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아파서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아파서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">apaseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because I'm sick / it hurts</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_tired.webp\" alt=\"피곤해서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('피곤해서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">피곤해서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">pigonhaeseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because I'm tired</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_hungry.webp\" alt=\"배고파서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배고파서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">배고파서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">baegopaseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because I'm hungry</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_busy.webp\" alt=\"바빠서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바빠서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">바빠서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bappaseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because I'm busy</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_fun.webp\" alt=\"재미있어서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('재미있어서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">재미있어서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jaemiisseoseo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because it's fun</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_snow.webp\" alt=\"추워서\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('추워서')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">추워서</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chuwo seo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">because it's cold</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아파서 약을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아파서 약을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm sick so I take medicine.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('피곤해서 일찍 자요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">피곤해서 일찍 자요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm tired so I sleep early.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('배고파서 김밥을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">배고파서 김밥을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm hungry so I eat kimbap.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바빠서 친구를 못 만나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">바빠서 친구를 못 만나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'm busy so I can't meet my friend.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래가 재미있어서 계속 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래가 재미있어서 계속 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The song is fun so I keep listening.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('추워서 코트를 입어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">추워서 코트를 입어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's cold so I wear a coat.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤝 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> every reason word already carries <b>-아서/어서</b>, so you can drop it straight in front of a result: <b>배고파서 먹어요</b> (hungry so I eat). Reason + result, done!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍜</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">오늘의 단어<small>Food &amp; weather · 떡볶이와 눈</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_tteokbokki.webp\" alt=\"떡볶이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">떡볶이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">tteokbokki</div><div class=\"vw-en\">spicy rice cakes (tteokbokki)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b11_snow.webp\" alt=\"눈\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('눈')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">눈</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nun</div><div class=\"vw-en\">snow</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Tteokbokki is spicy so I can't eat it well.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이는 맛있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">떡볶이는 맛있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Tteokbokki is delicious.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('눈이 와서 정말 추워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">눈이 와서 정말 추워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">It's snowing so it's really cold.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌶️ <b>한국 길거리 음식:</b> 떡볶이 is THE most famous Korean street food. Say <b>매워서</b> when it's too hot for you, and <b>맛있어서</b> when you love it!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-1] Reading — 매워서 (reason -아서)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-1] Reading — 매워서</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">다음 중 맞는 문장을 고르세요. (Choose the correct sentence.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 매워서 = it's spicy, so I can't eat it well.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 떡볶이는 매워서요 잘 못 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 매워서요 is a polite ender, not a reason link.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 떡볶이는 맵서 잘 못 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 맵다 stem must become 매워서, not 맵서.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 떡볶이는 매워고 잘 못 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -고 links a list; -아서 gives the reason.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">매워서</span> = 맵다 (to be spicy) in its <b class=\"hl\">reason</b> form. Because it's spicy, <b class=\"hl\">I can't eat it well</b> — reason first, result after.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">매워서요</b> wrongly adds the polite 요, <b class=\"hl\">맵서</b> forgets the ㅂ-irregular change, and <b class=\"hl\">-고</b> just lists instead of giving a cause.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 ㅂ-stem 맵다 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">매워서</span> (like 춥다 → 추워서).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-2] Reading — 왜 그래요? (choose reason)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-2] Reading — 왜 그래요?</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">밖에 눈이 와요. (　) 저는 밖에 안 나가요. — Choose the reason.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 따뜻해서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 따뜻해서 means \"because it's warm\" — not why you'd stay in.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 추워서<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 추워서 = \"because it's cold\" — it snowed, so it's cold!</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 배고파서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 배고파서 means \"because I'm hungry\" — no food here.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 재미있어서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 재미있어서 means \"because it's fun\" — a reason to go OUT.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">When it snows it gets cold, so you stay inside. The reason is <span class=\"pt-ko\">추워서</span> (because it's cold).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">따뜻해서</b> (warm) and <b class=\"hl\">재미있어서</b> (fun) would push you to GO OUT, and <b class=\"hl\">배고파서</b> (hungry) has nothing to do with the snow.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Read the situation first — \"밖에 눈이 와요\" (snow is falling) points straight to <span class=\"pt-ko\">추워서</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-3] Reading — 잘 못 (can't well)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-3] Reading — 잘 못 (can't well)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"저는 매운 음식을 잘 못 먹어요.\" — What does the speaker mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He can't eat spicy food well.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 잘 못 먹어요 = can't eat it WELL.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He only eats spicy food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ He struggles with it, he doesn't love it.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> He is cooking spicy food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ There is no cooking here.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Spicy food makes him angry.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No anger is mentioned.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">잘 못 먹어요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">잘</b> (well) + <b class=\"hl\">못</b> (can't) + 먹어요 (eat) → \"I <b class=\"hl\">can't eat it well</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ He doesn't only eat spicy food, isn't cooking, and isn't angry — he just finds it hard to eat.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">못</span> = can't; add <span class=\"pt-ko\">잘</span> to mean \"can't do it WELL (but I try)\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-4] Reading — -고 (and)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-4] Reading — -고 (and)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"저는 노래를 듣고 춤을 춰요.\" — What does this mean?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I dance, so I listen to music.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -고 links two things; it doesn't give a reason.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> I listen to music and dance.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 듣고 = listen and, then 춤을 춰요 = I dance.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I can't listen or dance.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ There is no 잘 못 here — both actions happen.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> The music is too loud.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No volume is mentioned.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">노래를 듣<b class=\"hl\">고</b> 춤을 춰요</span> = \"I listen to music <b class=\"hl\">and</b> I dance.\" The <b class=\"hl\">-고</b> just chains the two actions.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">-고</b> is for listing, NOT for giving a reason (that's -아서/어서).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Reason = <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아서/어서</span>. List of actions = <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고</span>. Don't mix them up!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-5] Reading — 고추도 먹고 (complete)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-5] Reading — 고추도 먹고 (complete)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">로이는 고추도 먹고 떡볶이도 (　). — Choose the correct verb.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ The last verb of the -고 list must be a normal ending, not -고 again.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹어서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -어서 means \"so/because\" — wrong for a list.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 못 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Roy CAN eat — there's no 잘 못 here.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q5',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 고추도 먹고 떡볶이도 먹어요 = eat peppers and tteokbokki.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In a <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고</span> list only the FIRST verb takes <b class=\"hl\">-고</b>; the final verb keeps its normal polite ending: <span class=\"pt-ko\">고추도 먹<b class=\"hl\">고</b> 떡볶이도 <b class=\"hl\">먹어요</b></span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">먹고</b> would leave the sentence unfinished, <b class=\"hl\">먹어서</b> turns it into a reason, and <b class=\"hl\">못 먹어요</b> says he can't (Roy eats everything!).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Only the LAST action gets the final ending <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아요/어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-6] Reading — 눈이 와서 추워요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-6] Reading — 눈이 와서 추워요</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"오늘은 눈이 와서 추워요. 그래서 저는 집에 있고 따뜻한 차를 마셔요.\" — Why does the speaker stay home?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Because it's cold outside.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 눈이 와서 = it snows, so... it's cold.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Because it's hot outside.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 따뜻한 is about the warm tea, not the weather.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Because Roy is coming.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No one is mentioned coming.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Because the music is fun.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ There's no music here.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The passage says <span class=\"pt-ko\">눈이 와<b class=\"hl\">서</b> 추워요</span> — \"it's snowing, <b class=\"hl\">so</b> it's cold\" — that is why the speaker stays home.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">따뜻한 차</b> (warm tea) is what they drink INSIDE; it is not why they stay. And no Roy or music appears.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Spot the reason word ending in <span class=\"pt-ko\">-아서/어서</span>: it tells you the CAUSE.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-7] Listening — 아파서 병원에 가요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-7] Listening — 아파서 병원에 가요</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('아파서 병원에 가요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 Listen. Why is the person going to the hospital?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> They are sick.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 아파서 = because I'm sick.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> They are cold.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 추워서 (cold) wasn't said.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> They are hungry.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 배고파서 (hungry) wasn't said.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> They are busy.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 바빠서 (busy) wasn't said.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">아파<b class=\"hl\">서</b> 병원에 가요</span> — \"because I'm <b class=\"hl\">sick</b>, I go to the hospital.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 추워서/배고파서/바빠서 are other reasons the hospital doesn't fix.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for the key first word ending in -아서/어서 — that's the reason.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-8] Listening — 김치를 잘 못 먹어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-8] Listening — 김치를 잘 못 먹어요</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 김치를 잘 못 먹어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 Listen. What does the speaker say about kimchi?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> They love spicy kimchi.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ They say they can't eat it well, not that they love it.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> They are cooking kimchi.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No cooking is mentioned.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> They can't eat kimchi well.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 잘 못 먹어요 = can't eat it well.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Kimchi is not spicy at all.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Nothing about the spice level.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 김치를 <b class=\"hl\">잘 못</b> 먹어요</span> = \"I can't eat kimchi <b class=\"hl\">well</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ They don't love it, cook it, or judge its spice — they simply have a hard time eating it.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">잘 못 + verb</span> = \"I can't do it well (but I try).\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-9] Listening — 떡볶이 (summary)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-9] Listening — 떡볶이 (summary)</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('떡볶이는 매워서 잘 못 먹어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 Listen. Which is the best summary?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Tteokbokki is spicy, so I can't eat it well.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ That is the whole meaning of the sentence.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Tteokbokki is sweet, so I eat a lot.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ It's spicy (매워서), not sweet.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> I can't cook tteokbokki.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Eating, not cooking.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> It's cold, so I don't go out.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No weather in this sentence.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence <span class=\"pt-ko\">떡볶이는 매워<b class=\"hl\">서</b> 잘 못 먹어요</span> = tteokbokki is <b class=\"hl\">spicy</b>, so I <b class=\"hl\">can't eat it well</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It's not sweet or cold, and nothing is about cooking.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 This is THE unit sentence — it packs -아서 (reason) + 잘 못 (can't well) together.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[11-10] Listening — 왜 못 만나요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">[11-10] Listening — 왜 못 만나요?</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('미안해요. 저는 오늘 아파서 밖에 못 나가요. 그래서 친구를 못 만나요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 Listen. Why can't the person meet their friend today?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u11q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Because they are tired.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 피곤해서 wasn't said — it's 아파서.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Because they are sick.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 아파서 = because I'm sick, so I can't go out.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Because they are busy.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 바빠서 wasn't said.</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u11q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Because it's snowing.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 추워서/눈 weren't said.</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u11q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘 아파<b class=\"hl\">서</b> 밖에 못 나가요</span> — \"today, <b class=\"hl\">because I'm sick</b>, I can't go out.\" So they can't meet their friend.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 피곤해서 (tired), 바빠서 (busy) and 추워서 (cold) are all wrong reasons here.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Chain two reasons with -아서 on each: <span class=\"pt-ko\">아파서 못 나가요</span> = sick, so I can't go out.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🍜 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>먹방 — The Eating Show!</h3>\n    <p>K-POP idols often appear on <b>먹방</b> (mukbang / eating shows) where they eat on camera. When the food is too spicy, idols famously cry out <b>매워서 잘 못 먹어요!</b> — and fans find it adorable.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🌶️ '매워서' is a real-life reason word — use it the next time you face 떡볶이 and need to say, politely, \"It's too spicy for me!\"</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 12, "title": "I'd like to look at some sneakers", "en": "운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요", "theme": "shopping", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 12 · SHOPPING &amp; WANTS</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">12</div><div><h2>I&rsquo;d Like to Look at Some Sneakers</h2><div class=\"en\">운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요 — Shopping · -고 싶어요 / 좀 / -아/어 주세요</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 12/20</span>\n      <h3>채아의 팝업 스토어 — \"사고 싶어요!\"</h3>\n      <p>글로시스의 <b>팝업 스토어</b>에서 채아가 새 <b>운동화</b>를 찾아요. 팬사인회에 신고 싶어서요! \"운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요.\" — 점원에게 웃으며 말해요. 💛</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">At the Glowsis <b>pop-up store</b>, <b>Chaea</b> looks for new <b>sneakers</b> — she wants to wear them at the fansign! \"운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요 (I&rsquo;d like to look at some sneakers).\" she says to the clerk with a smile. 💛</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 12/20 획득 — Shopping &amp; wants!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🛍️</span> Shop for clothes &amp; shoes</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💭</span> -고 싶어요 (want to)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🙏</span> 좀 &amp; -아/어 주세요 politely</div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 12 — At the Pop-up Store</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🛍️ Glowsis merch shop</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">저기요, 운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Excuse me, I&rsquo;d like to look at some sneakers.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">점원 다희</div><div class=\"ko\">네! 어떤 사이즈를 원하세요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Sure! What size would you like?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">240이에요. 저 옆에 있는 거 보여 주세요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Size 240. Please show me the ones over there.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">점원 다희</div><div class=\"ko\">이 티셔츠도 같이 볼까요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Would you like to look at this t-shirt too?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 이거 사고 싶어요. 사 주세요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! I want to buy these. Please ring me up!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">팬사인회에 그 운동화 신고 올게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I&rsquo;ll wear those sneakers to the fansign!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 싶어요 — \"I want to ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Take any verb stem and add <b>고 싶어요</b> to say what you <b>want to do</b>. Want to buy sneakers? 사다 → 사<b>고 싶어요</b>. It works on every verb!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">새 운동화를 사<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to buy new sneakers.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">그 티셔츠를 입어 보<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to try on that t-shirt.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">팬사인회에 가<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to go to the fansign.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">좀 — \"a bit / a little\" (and politely softens a request)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>좀</b> comes right before a verb or a phrase to say <b>a little / a bit</b>. In a shop it also makes a request sound <b>polite and gentle</b> — it takes the edge off!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">운동화를 <b>좀</b> 보고 싶어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I&rsquo;d like to look at some sneakers (a bit).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">치마가 <b>좀</b> 작아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">The skirt is a little small.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>좀</b> 봐 주세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Could you show me a little, please?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 주세요 — \"please ~ (for me)\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Ask someone to <b>do something for you</b>: verb stem + <b>아/어 주세요</b>. Stem vowel ㅏ/ㅗ → <b>아 주세요</b>; other vowels → <b>어 주세요</b>; 하다 verbs → <b>해 주세요</b>. A must-have at the cash register!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 옷을 보여 <b>주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please show me this outfit.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이거 사 <b>주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please buy this for me.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">사이즈 좀 봐 <b>주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please check the size for me.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher&rsquo;s Deep-Dive · putting \"운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요\" together</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I&rsquo;d like to look at some sneakers.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why do shoppers say <b>보고 싶어요</b> and slip in <b>좀</b> — and when would you switch to <b>주세요</b>?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">싶어요</span> sticks onto the verb stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">보-</span> (보다 = to look) with <b>고</b> to say you <b>want</b> to do it: <b>보고 싶어요</b> = \"I want to look.\" The word <span class=\"pt-ko\">좀</span> adds \"a little,\" so <span class=\"pt-ko\">좀 보고 싶어요</span> feels like \"I&rsquo;d <i>like</i> to take a look\" — softer than a blunt demand. <b>좀</b> is a magic politeness button in shops.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">운동화<b>를</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">sneakers <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">를 = object particle. The thing you want to look at comes first.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">좀</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">a little <span class=\"t-sub\">(softener)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Makes the wish gentle &amp; polite — \"some sneakers,\" \"a bit.\"</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">보고 싶어요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">want to look <span class=\"t-sub\">(보- + 고 싶어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Stem 보- + 고 + 싶어요. Same pattern: 사고 싶어요 (want to buy).</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-고 싶어요 = \"I want to ~\"</b> — build it from any verb stem: <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span> → <b>가고 싶어요</b>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> → <b>사고 싶어요</b>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">입다</span> → <b>입고 싶어요</b>. Throw in <b>좀</b> before the verb and your wish turns into a polite shopper&rsquo;s request.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Want (my own wish)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">운동화를 <b>좀 보고 싶어요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"I&rsquo;d like to look at some sneakers.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Ask a helper (please do)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">이거 <b>보여 주세요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">\"Please show me this.\" — -아/어 주세요</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>want</b> = you + 싶어요; <b>please</b> = ask + 주세요. In an idol merch shop line you might say <span class=\"pt-ko\">그 운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요</span>, then hand over money and add <span class=\"pt-ko\">이거 사 주세요!</span> Practice the pair — you&rsquo;ll use them at every pop-up store!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👟</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">신발<small>Footwear · 신고 싶어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_shoe.webp\" alt=\"운동화\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운동화')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">운동화</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">undonghwa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">sneakers / running shoes</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_shoe.webp\" alt=\"신발\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('신발')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">신발</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sinbal</div><div class=\"vw-en\">shoes</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear in a shop</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('새 운동화를 사고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">새 운동화를 사고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to buy new sneakers.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 신발 좀 봐 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 신발 좀 봐 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please let me look at these shoes.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운동화가 편해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">운동화가 편해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Sneakers are comfortable.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👟 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 신발 is any shoe; <b>운동화</b> = sports shoes / sneakers. Both take <b>을/를</b> as the object of 사다 (buy).</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👕</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">옷과 옷가지<small>Clothing · 입고 싶어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_tshirt.webp\" alt=\"옷\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('옷')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">옷</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ot</div><div class=\"vw-en\">clothes</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_tshirt.webp\" alt=\"티셔츠\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('티셔츠')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">티셔츠</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">tisyeocheu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">t-shirt</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_pants.webp\" alt=\"바지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('바지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">바지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">baji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">pants</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_skirt.webp\" alt=\"치마\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치마')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">치마</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chima</div><div class=\"vw-en\">skirt</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear in a shop</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('티셔츠가 너무 예뻐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">티셔츠가 너무 예뻐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The t-shirt is so pretty.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 바지는 어때요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 바지는 어때요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How about these pants?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치마를 입고 싶어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치마를 입고 싶어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I want to wear a skirt.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('옷이 마음에 들어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">옷이 마음에 들어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I like the clothes.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👕 <b>입는 것:</b> 웃 upper / lower all = <b>옷</b> (clothes). Pants = <b>바지</b>, skirt = <b>치마</b>, and a casual tee = <b>티셔츠</b>. To \"put on\" clothes you <b>입어요</b>.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🛍️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">쇼핑 준비물<small>Shopping basics · 뭐를 살까요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_bag.webp\" alt=\"가방\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가방')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가방</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gabang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bag</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_size.webp\" alt=\"사이즈\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사이즈')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사이즈</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">saijeu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">size</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear in a shop</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가방이 크네요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가방이 크네요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The bag is big.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어느 사이즈예요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어느 사이즈예요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What size is it?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 사이즈 있어요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 사이즈 있어요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Do you have this size?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🛍️ <b>살 때:</b> check the <b>사이즈</b> (size), try it, then <b>사고 싶어요</b>. A <b>가방</b> (bag) holds what you buy!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-1] Reading — 사고 싶어요 (-고 싶어요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that means &ldquo;I want to buy new sneakers.&rdquo;</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q1\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>새 운동화를 사고 싶어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 사고 + 싶어요 = want to buy sneakers</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>새 운동화를 사고 좋아요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 좋아요 isn&rsquo;t the want ending</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>새 운동화를 사고 주세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 주세요 asks someone else to do it</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>새 운동화를 사고 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 있어요 = &ldquo;have / is there&rdquo;</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-고 싶어요</b> = &ldquo;I want to ~.&rdquo; Take the verb <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> (buy) → stem <b class=\"hl\">사-</b> → add <b class=\"hl\">고 싶어요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">주세요</b> is a polite request to a helper, not your own wish; <b class=\"hl\">좋아요</b> means &ldquo;good/like.&rdquo;</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Pattern: <span class=\"pt-ko\">Verb stem + 고 싶어요</span> — 사다→사고 싶어요, 보다→보고 싶어요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-2] Reading — Vocab — 운동화</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read: <span class=\"pt-ko\">새 운동화가 있어요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(new + ______)</span> — what is 운동화?</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q2\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>new t-shirt<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 새 티셔츠</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>new sneakers<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 운동화 = sneakers / running shoes</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>new skirt<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 새 치마</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>new bag<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 새 가방</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화</span> = <b class=\"hl\">sneakers / running shoes</b> — sporty shoes you wear to move.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">티셔츠</b> (t-shirt), <b class=\"hl\">치마</b> (skirt), <b class=\"hl\">가방</b> (bag) are different shopping words.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 General word for any shoe is <span class=\"pt-ko\">신발</span>; <span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화</span> is specifically sports shoes.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-3] Reading — 좀 (polite)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence politely asks a clerk to show you some sneakers?</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q3\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span><span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 좀 softens the wish to &ldquo;some/a bit&rdquo;</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span><span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화를 보고 싶어요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no 좀, more direct</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span><span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화를 좀 봐 주세요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 좀 + 봐 주세요 = a gentle polite request</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span><span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화 좀 사 주세요.</span><span class=\"o-gl\">❌ asks to buy, not to look</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The most polite shopper line = <b class=\"hl\">좀</b> (a little) + <b class=\"hl\">봐 주세요</b> (please look): <span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화를 좀 봐 주세요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Adding <b class=\"hl\">좀</b> before the verb makes any request gentle — it&rsquo;s the secret to sounding polite in Korean shops.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 옵션 1 says your own wish (want to look); 옵션 3 politely asks a helper — that is what &ldquo;please&rdquo; needs.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-4] Reading — Vocab — 옷</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read: <span class=\"pt-ko\">이 옷이 너무 예뻐요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(this ______ is so pretty)</span> — what is 옷?</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q4\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>shoes<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 신발</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>clothes<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 옷 = clothes in general</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>pants<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 바지</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>skirt<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is 치마</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In <span class=\"pt-ko\">새 옷</span> = &ldquo;new <b class=\"hl\">clothes</b>,&rdquo; so <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷</span> means clothes.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">바지</b> (pants), <b class=\"hl\">치마</b> (skirt), <b class=\"hl\">신발</b> (shoes) are specific items inside the bigger group <b class=\"hl\">옷</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Buy &ldquo;옷&rdquo; and it could be a <span class=\"pt-ko\">티셔츠</span>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">바지</span>, or <span class=\"pt-ko\">치마</span>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-5] Listening — 가방을 사고 싶어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the speaker wants to buy.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 가방을 사고 싶어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q5\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>가방 (bag)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 사고 싶어요 = want to buy a bag</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>바지 (pants)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not the item heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>치마 (skirt)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not the item heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>신발 (shoes)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not the item heard</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 가방을 사고 싶어요</span> — the speaker wants to <b class=\"hl\">buy a bag</b> (가방).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The key noun is <b class=\"hl\">가방</b>; the ending <span class=\"pt-ko\">사고 싶어요</span> = &ldquo;want to buy.&rdquo;</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 In listening, catch the <b>noun</b> first, then the <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고 싶어요</span> ending.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-6] Listening — 치마를 보여 주세요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what is being asked.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('치마를 좀 보여 주세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q6\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>buy me a t-shirt<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ you hear 보여 주세요, not 사 주세요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>buy me the skirt<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 사 주세요 means buy for me, not heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>show me a bag<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the item heard is 치마 (skirt), not 가방</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q6',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>show me the skirt<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 치마를 보여 주세요 = please show the skirt</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">치마를 보여 주세요</span> = &ldquo;Please <b class=\"hl\">show</b> me the skirt.&rdquo; 보여 주다 = to show (for me).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">보여 주세요</b> (show) ≠ <b class=\"hl\">사 주세요</b> (buy for me) — two different polite requests.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -아/어 주세요 turns any verb into &ldquo;please ~ for me&rdquo;: 보이다→보여 주세요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-7] Reading — 보여 주세요 (-아/어 주세요)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the polite request: &ldquo;Please show me this outfit.&rdquo;</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q7\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>봐 주세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 보다→봐 주세요 is to look, but here to show</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>보여 주세요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 보여 주세요 = please show me</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>보고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is &ldquo;want to look&rdquo;, a wish not a request</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ plain statement, not polite please</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To ask a clerk to <b class=\"hl\">show</b> you something, the verb is <span class=\"pt-ko\">보여 주다</span> → <b class=\"hl\">보여 주세요</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">봐 주세요</b> means &ldquo;please look (for me)&rdquo; and <b class=\"hl\">보고 싶어요</b> is your own wish — not a request to a helper.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Show me this outfit: <span class=\"pt-ko\">이 옷을 보여 주세요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-8] Reading — Vocab — 티셔츠</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read: <span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스가 이 티셔츠에 사인해요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(Glowsis signs this ______)</span> — what is it?</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q8\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>티셔츠<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 티셔츠 = t-shirt, the top being signed</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>바지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 바지 = pants</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>치마<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 치마 = skirt</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>가방<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 가방 = bag</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The members will sign <span class=\"pt-ko\">티셔츠</span> = <b class=\"hl\">t-shirt</b> — a casual top fans love to wear.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">바지</b> (pants) and <b class=\"hl\">치마</b> (skirt) are bottoms, not a top you&rsquo;d sign on the chest.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 티셔츠 = English &ldquo;t-shirt&rdquo; in Korean letters!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-9] Reading — comprehension — what Chaea wants</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Passage: <span class=\"pt-ko\">채아는 팝업 스토어에서 운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요. 사이즈는 240이에요.</span> <span class=\"gl\">(Chaea wants to look at some sneakers at the pop-up store. Her size is 240.)</span> — What does Chaea want?</div>\n\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q9\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>그녀는 바지를 원해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ she wants sneakers, not pants</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>그녀는 운동화를 원해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ she says 운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>그녀는 티셔츠를 사요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ she only wants to look, not stated buying</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>그녀는 사이즈를 몰라요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ she knows her size (240)</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">채아 says <span class=\"pt-ko\">운동화를 좀 보고 싶어요</span> — she wants to look at <b class=\"hl\">sneakers (운동화)</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 바지 (pants) isn&rsquo;t mentioned; buying the t-shirt &amp; knowing size 240 are details not matching her wish.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 The <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고 싶어요</span> tells us what she <b>wants</b> — read for that core wish.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[12-10] Listening — 글로시스 티셔츠</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose what the fan wants.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('글로시스 티셔츠를 사고 싶어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u12q10\"><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>그녀는 가방을 사요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ she only wants, and not a bag</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>그녀는 티셔츠를 원해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 사고 싶어요 = want to buy a t-shirt</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>그녀는 치마를 입어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u12q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>그녀는 바지를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not heard</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u12q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You hear <span class=\"pt-ko\">글로시스 티셔츠를 사고 싶어요</span> = &ldquo;I want to <b class=\"hl\">buy a Glowsis t-shirt</b>.&rdquo;</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options name bags/skirts/pants — none are in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> + <span class=\"pt-ko\">고 싶어요</span> = want to buy. A fan&rsquo;s most-used phrase at merch!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Idol Merch &amp; Fansign Shopping!</h3>\n    <p>At a K-pop <b>pop-up store</b> you say <b>사고 싶어요</b> to ask for merch, and at a <b>팬사인회 (fansign)</b> idols ask fans what they bought. Knowing how to want &amp; request politely = shopping superpower!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ At the counter try: \"<b>이 티셔츠를 사고 싶어요. 사이즈 좀 봐 주세요!</b>\" — then \"<b>이거 사 주세요!</b>\"</div>\n  </div>\n"}]}, {"id": 13, "title": "Can you do K-pop dance?", "en": "케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요?", "theme": "ability", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 13 · ABILITIES</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">13</div><div><h2>Can you do K-pop dance?</h2><div class=\"en\">케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요? — Abilities · -(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 / 못 / -지만</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 1B — CAN &amp; CAN'T</span>\n      <h3>우리는 무엇을 할 수 있어요? — \"할 수 있어요!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘 글로시스는 <b>재능 챌린지</b>를 해요. 각자 무엇을 할 수 있는지, 못 하는지 말해요. \"케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요!\" — 네 명의 재능이 모이면 무대가 완성돼요! 💪</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today Glowsis is doing a <b>talent challenge</b>. Each member says what they can and can't do. \"케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요!\" (I can do K-pop dance!) — when the four talents come together, the stage is complete! 💪</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💪 GLOW POINT 획득 — \"할 수 있어요!\"</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💪</span> Say what you can do</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚫</span> Say what you can't do (못)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤸</span> Connect with -지만 (but)</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 13 — Talent Challenge</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏋️ Practice room talent show</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요. 그리고 노래도 부를 수 있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I can do K-pop dance. And I can sing too!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 한국어를 할 수 있어요. 운전도 할 수 있어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I can speak Korean. I can drive too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 발레를 못 해요. 하지만 요리는 잘할 수 있어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I can't do ballet. But I can cook well!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">저는 기타는 칠 수 있어요. 그런데 테니스는 못 쳐요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I can play the guitar. But I can't play tennis.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 모두 할 수 있어요! 함께면 못 하는 게 없어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">We can all do it! Together, there's nothing we can't do!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요 — \"can / be able to\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">After a verb stem, add <b>(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</b> to say \"I can ~\". After a final consonant use <b>을 수 있어요</b> (먹다 → 먹<b>을 수 있어요</b>); after a vowel add <b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b> (추다 → 추<b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b>). It expresses ability.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">춤을 출 <b>수 있어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can dance. (추다 + ㄹ 수 있어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">한국어를 할 <b>수 있어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can speak Korean.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">케이팝 댄스를 출 <b>수 있어요</b>?</span><span class=\"gl\">Can you do K-pop dance?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">못 — \"can't\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Place <b>못</b> right before an action verb to say \"can't do it\": <b>못 해요</b> = \"I can't (do)\". This is the negative of ability — the opposite of <b>-(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">발레를 <b>못 해요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't do ballet.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">운전을 <b>못 해요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't drive.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">노래를 <b>못</b> 불러요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can't sing.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-지만 — \"but\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-지만</b> to a verb or adjective stem to connect two ideas with \"but\". Put the first fact, then -지만, then the second fact. A favorite for talents and limits!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">요리는 잘하<b>지만</b> 발레는 못 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I cook well, but I can't do ballet.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">기타는 칠 수 있<b>지만</b> 테니스는 못 쳐요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I can play guitar, but I can't play tennis.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">춤은 잘 추<b>지만</b> 노래는 못 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I dance well, but I can't sing.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Can you do K-pop dance?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">How does an idol say \"I can\" — and how do you build the question <b>출 수 있어요?</b> step by step?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Ability in Korean is built with three pieces: the action verb stem, the <b>(으)ㄹ 수</b> part (the \"-able\" idea), and the polite <b>있어요</b> (\"there is\" → there IS ability). For the verb\n      <b>추다</b> (to dance), strip to the stem <b>추</b>, it ends in a vowel ㅜ, so we attach <b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b> → <b>출 수 있어요</b>. Then just add the object:\n      <b>케이팝 댄스를 출 수 있어요</b> = \"I can do K-pop dance.\" Raise the tone at the end and it becomes the question \"Can you…?\"\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">춤을 추<b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I can dance <span class=\"t-sub\">(vowel + ㄹ)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">춤 = dance (noun, object with 을). 추다 (to dance) stem 추 ends in ㅜ → add ㄹ 수 있어요.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">vs</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹<b>을 수 있어요</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I can eat <span class=\"t-sub\">(consonant + 을)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">먹다 (to eat) stem 먹 ends in the consonant ㄱ → add 을 수 있어요.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">못 해요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">I can't <span class=\"t-sub\">(no ability)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">The simple negative of ability. Put 못 right before the verb. 운전을 못 해요 = I can't drive.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-지만 = \"but\"</b> — glue two talents or a talent + a limit together. <b>춤은 잘 추지만 노래는 못 해요</b> = \"I dance well, but I can't sing.\" Use it to be honest about your skills, just like idols in fan chats.\n    Pick <b>을 수 있어요</b> after a final consonant (먹다→먹을 수 있어요) and <b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b> after a vowel (추다→출 수 있어요, 가다→갈 수 있어요).\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Final consonant (받침) → 을 수 있어요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">먹<b>을 수 있어요</b> · 읽<b>을 수 있어요</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">받침 = ㄱ·ㄴ·ㅁ… → \"I can eat / I can read.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>No consonant (vowel) → ㄹ 수 있어요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">추<b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b> · 가<b>ㄹ 수 있어요</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">No 받침 = ㅜ·ㅏ… → \"I can dance / I can go.\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> ability = verb stem + <b>(으)ㄹ 수 있어요</b>, and to flip it to \"can't\" just say <b>못</b> + verb. To show contrast, drop in <b>-지만</b> (but). Now fill your own talent list —\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 ○○을/를 할 수 있어요. 하지만 ○○은/는 못 해요</span> — and join Glowsis's talent challenge!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎤</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">무대 재능<small>Stage talents · 무엇을 할 수 있어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_dance.webp\" alt=\"춤\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('춤')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">춤</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chum</div><div class=\"vw-en\">dance</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u1_song.webp\" alt=\"노래\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">노래</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">norae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">song</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b13_ballet.webp\" alt=\"발레\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('발레')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">발레</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">balle</div><div class=\"vw-en\">ballet</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b13_guitar.webp\" alt=\"기타\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기타')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">기타</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gita</div><div class=\"vw-en\">guitar</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 춤을 출 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 춤을 출 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can dance.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('노래를 부를 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">노래를 부를 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can sing.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('발레는 못 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">발레는 못 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can't do ballet.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기타를 칠 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">기타를 칠 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can play the guitar.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎤 <b>무대 재능:</b> 춤(추다)·노래(부르다)·발레(하다)·기타(치다). Add <b>을/ㄹ 수 있어요</b> after the stem: 추다→출 수 있어요, 칠 수 있어요.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💪</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">생활과 스포츠 능력<small>Life &amp; sports · 무슨 재주가 있어요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u2_korean.webp\" alt=\"한국어\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국어')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">한국어</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hangugeo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Korean</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b13_drive.webp\" alt=\"운전\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운전')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">운전</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">unjeon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">driving</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b13_cook2.webp\" alt=\"요리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">요리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yori</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cooking</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b13_tennis.webp\" alt=\"테니스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('테니스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">테니스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">teniseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">tennis</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('한국어를 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">한국어를 할 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can speak Korean.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('운전을 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">운전을 할 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can drive.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('요리를 잘할 수 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">요리를 잘할 수 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can cook well.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('테니스는 못 쳐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">테니스는 못 쳐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I can't play tennis.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💪 <b>생활 능력:</b> 한국어(하다)·운전(하다)·요리(하다)·테니스(치다). With 하다 verbs say <b>할 수 있어요</b> / <b>못 해요</b>.</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-1] Reading — 출 수 있어요 (ㄹ 수 있어요)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form of \"can\".</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">케이팝 댄스는 열심히 연습해서 지금은 다 (　) 수 있어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 출<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 추다 stem 추 ends in a vowel → 출 수 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 추을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 추다 has no final consonant, so no 을</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 추<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ missing the ㄹ 수 있어요 ending</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 춤을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 춤을 is the object, not the ability form</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">We need \"can dance\" from <b class=\"hl\">추다</b>. Its stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">추</span> ends in a vowel (ㅜ), so we add <b class=\"hl\">ㄹ 수 있어요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">출 수 있어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">추을</b> would need a 받침 that 추다 doesn't have; <b class=\"hl\">춤을</b> is the object phrase, not the verb ending.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Vowel stem + ㄹ 수 있어요 → <span class=\"pt-ko\">추다</span> = <span class=\"pt-ko\">출 수 있어요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-2] Reading — 먹을 수 있어요 (을 수 있어요)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct ability form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">저는 김치를 아주 잘 (　) 수 있어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹을<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 먹다 stem 먹 ends in consonant ㄱ → 을 수 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ need the 을 수 있어요 ending</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹ㄹ<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no bare ㄹ form after a consonant</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹기<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 먹기 is the noun form</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다</span> (to eat) has the stem <b class=\"hl\">먹</b> ending in the consonant ㄱ (받침), so we attach <b class=\"hl\">을 수 있어요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹을 수 있어요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Consonant stems never take the bare ㄹ form; they need the full <b class=\"hl\">을</b> first.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 받침(consonant) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹을 수 있어요</span>, like <span class=\"pt-ko\">읽을 수 있어요</span> (can read).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-3] Reading — 못 해요 (can't)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the sentence that means \"I can't drive\".</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which one says \"I can't drive\"?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 운전을 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 못 + 해요 = can't do; 운전을 못 해요 = I can't drive</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 운전을 할 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ This says I CAN drive</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 운전해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Just \"I drive\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 운전을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ I like driving</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To say \"can't\", put <b class=\"hl\">못</b> right before the verb: <span class=\"pt-ko\">운전을 못 해요</span> = \"I can't drive.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">할 수 있어요</b> is the POSITIVE \"can\", not the negative.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">할 수 있어요</span> (can) vs <span class=\"pt-ko\">못 해요</span> (can't) — the two sides of ability.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-4] Reading — -지만 (but)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct connector meaning \"but\".</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">노래는 잘해요. (　) 춤은 못 춰요. — pick the word that means \"but\".</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 하지만<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 하지만 = but, linking the two ideas</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 그리고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 그리고 = and</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 그래서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 그래서 = so / therefore</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 그런데요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ polite filler, not the connector</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Use <b class=\"hl\">하지만</b> (but) to connect two contrasting ideas: I sing well, <b class=\"hl\">but</b> I can't dance.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">그리고</b> means \"and\" and <b class=\"hl\">그래서</b> means \"so\" — neither gives a contrast.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Inside one sentence you can also glue the verb with <b class=\"hl\">-지만</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">잘해<span class=\"hl\">지만</span></span> 춤은 못 춰요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-5] Reading — 운전 (can comprehension)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"아란 씨는 운전을 할 수 있어요.\" — 아란 씨는 무엇을 할 수 있어요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 운전<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You read 운전을 할 수 있어요 = can drive</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 요리<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not cooking here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 춤<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not dance here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 테니스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not tennis here</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence says <span class=\"pt-ko\">운전을 할 수 있어요</span> — Aran <b class=\"hl\">can drive</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 요리/춤/테니스 are other talents not mentioned in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 For \"what can they do\", the answer is the object right before <b class=\"hl\">할 수 있어요</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-6] Reading — -지만 comprehension]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"저는 요리를 잘할 수 있어요. 하지만 발레는 못 해요.\" — 요리는 어때요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 잘할 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ He CAN cook well — the first clause</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ The 못 is about ballet, not cooking</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 할 수 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ He can cook</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 하기 싫어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not about wanting to</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The first clause says <span class=\"pt-ko\">요리를 잘할 수 있어요</span> (I can cook well). The <b class=\"hl\">하지만</b> (but) only limits the next clause, ballet.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The <b class=\"hl\">못 해요</b> applies to 발레 (ballet), so it is not about cooking.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 After <b class=\"hl\">-지만</b> the sign can flip — keep each talent with its own clause.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-7] Listening — 한국어를 할 수 있어요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the person can do.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 한국어를 할 수 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What can the speaker do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 한국어<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 한국어를 할 수 있어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 요리<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not cooking</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 발레<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not ballet</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 운전<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not driving</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">저는 한국어를 할 수 있어요</span> = \"I can speak <b class=\"hl\">Korean</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 요리/발레/운전 are abilities not mentioned in the clip.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 하다 verbs use <b class=\"hl\">할 수 있어요</b>: 한국어를 할 수 있어요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-8] Listening — 발레를 못 해요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the person can't do.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 기타는 칠 수 있어요. 하지만 발레는 못 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What can't the speaker do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 발레<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 발레는 못 해요 = can't do ballet</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 기타<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Guitar he CAN play</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 노래<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not said as can't</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 요리<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not said as can't</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker <b class=\"hl\">can play guitar</b> (칠 수 있어요) but <b class=\"hl\">can't do ballet</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">발레는 못 해요</span>). The question asks what they can't do.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">기타</b> is the thing they CAN do — the opposite of what's asked.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Watch the <b class=\"hl\">하지만</b> (but): after it the ability turns negative — 발레는 못 해요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-9] Listening — 요리 (지만)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best answer.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 테니스는 못 쳐요. 하지만 요리는 잘할 수 있어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Which is true about the speaker?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 요리를 잘할 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ After 하지만, cooking is the CAN skill</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 테니스를 잘 쳐요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Tennis is 못 쳐요 = can't</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 아무것도 못 해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ They can cook well</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 춤을 출 수 있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Dance not mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker <b class=\"hl\">can't play tennis</b> but <b class=\"hl\">can cook well</b> (<span class=\"pt-ko\">요리를 잘할 수 있어요</span>). So the true statement is about cooking.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Tennis is the negative (<span class=\"pt-ko\">못 쳐요</span>), so \"잘 쳐요\" is false.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Use <b class=\"hl\">-지만</b> to pair a limit (못) with a strength (할 수 있어요).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[13-10] Listening — abilities summary]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('저는 노래는 부를 수 있어요. 춤도 출 수 있어요. 운전은 못 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What can this person do?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u13q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 노래와 춤<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Both singing and dancing are CAN skills</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 노래와 운전<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Driving is 못 해요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 춤과 운전<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Driving is not possible</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u13q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 요리와 노래<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Cooking not mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u13q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker can <b class=\"hl\">sing</b> (노래는 부를 수 있어요) and <b class=\"hl\">dance</b> (춤도 출 수 있어요), but <b class=\"hl\">can't drive</b> (운전은 못 해요). The best summary is \"sing and dance\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Anything with 운전 is wrong, because driving is the one thing they can't do.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 To summarize, sort each talent into <b class=\"hl\">can</b> (수 있어요) vs <b class=\"hl\">can't</b> (못).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Talent Challenge, Like an Idol!</h3>\n    <p>At auditions and fan meets, idols show off what they can do. Idols love saying <b>\"○○을/를 할 수 있어요!\"</b> — and honest idols also admit <b>\"못 해요\"</b> with a smile, then add a <b>하지만</b>!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"저는 ○○을/를 할 수 있어요. 하지만 ○○은/는 못 해요.\" — Fill in two talents and one limit. Can you make a full idol talent introduction?</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 14, "title": "Before going home I'll travel", "en": "고향에 가기 전에 여행을 할 거예요", "theme": "plans", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 14 · PLANS & FUTURE</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">14</div><div><h2>Before Going Home I'll Travel</h2><div class=\"en\">고향에 가기 전에 여행을 할 거예요 — Plans & Future · -(으)ㄹ 거예요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 14/20</span>\n      <h3>채아의 컴백 계획 — \"다음 달에 컴백할 거예요!\"</h3>\n      <p>리더 <b>채아</b>는 팬들에게 <b>컴백 계획</b>을 알려요. \"다음 달에 컴백할 거예요!\" 팬들은 투어 예매를 준비해요. <b>고향</b>, <b>여행</b>, <b>휴가</b> — 글로시스의 달콤한 계획을 들어 봐요! 💜</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Leader <b>Chaea</b> shares <b>comeback plans</b> with the fans. \"We're making a comeback next month!\" Fans get ready to book the tour. <b>Hometown</b>, <b>travel</b>, <b>vacation</b> — come hear Glowsis's sweet plans! 💜</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 14/20 획득 — Future plans!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗓️</span> Talk about future plans</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎫</span> -(으)ㄹ 거예요 = will / I plan to</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🧳</span> -기 전에 & -고 나서 (before & after)</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 14 — Comeback Tour Plans</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📺 Practice room</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">다음 달에 글로시스가 컴백할 거예요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Glowsis is going to make a comeback next month!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">그 전에 전국 투어 계획을 세울 거예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Before that, we'll make a nationwide tour plan.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">부산에 가기 전에 서울 공연부터 해요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Let's do the Seoul show before going to Busan!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">콘서트를 하고 나서 휴가를 갈 거예요.</div><div class=\"gl\">After the concert I'll go on vacation.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">그래요! 휴가 때 고향에 갈 거예요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Right! Are you going to your hometown for vacation?</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요 — Will / Future plan</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Verb stem + <b>-ㄹ 거예요</b> (after a vowel) or <b>-을 거예요</b> (after a consonant) = \"will / plan to\". It's your intention or a strong plan, not just any future.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">갈 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm going to go (my plan).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">먹을 거예요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I'm going to eat.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">컴백할 거예요!</span><span class=\"gl\">We'll make a comeback!</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-기 전에 — Before doing</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Verb stem + <b>-기 전에</b> = \"before (doing)\". Add the -기 action first, then the main verb tells what comes after that moment.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">공연<b>하기 전에</b> 연습해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We practice before the performance.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">여행<b>가기 전에</b> 계획을 세워요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I make a plan before going on the trip.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밥을 먹<b>기 전에</b> 손을 씻어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I wash my hands before eating.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 나서 — After doing</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Verb stem + <b>-고 나서</b> = \"after (doing)\". Finish the first action, then do the next one. Use it to tell the order of plans.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">콘서트가 끝<b>나고 나서</b> 팬들을 만나요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We meet fans after the concert ends.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밥을 먹<b>고 나서</b> 커피를 마셔요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I drink coffee after eating.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">일<b>하고 나서</b> 집에 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I go home after working.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Why \"거예요\" means a plan</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">갈 거예요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"I'm going to go / I plan to go.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Idols say <b>컴백할 거예요</b> all the time. What does that little <b>거예요</b> really mean — and why isn't it just \"will\"?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      In English \"I will go\" is about the future. In Korean, <span class=\"pt-ko\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요</span> is built from a noun: <b>거</b> = <b>것</b> (\"thing\"),\n      so <span class=\"pt-ko\">갈 거예요</span> literally means <b>\"it is the thing that I'll go\"</b> — my plan, my intention, or a confident guess.\n      That's why it feels like a <b>promise or plan</b>, not a distant prediction.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">갈</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">will go <span class=\"t-sub\">(가다 + -ㄹ)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">가다 ends in the vowel ㅏ → add <b>-ㄹ</b>. After a consonant, add <b>-을</b> (먹다 → 먹<b>을</b> 거예요).</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">거</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">thing <span class=\"t-sub\">(것)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">거 is the spoken short form of 것. Written out formally it's 것이에요 — but Koreans say the smooth <b>거예요</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">예요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">= is <span class=\"t-sub\">(이다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">The whole ending = \"it is a thing I'll do\" = my plan. <b>거예요</b> = 것이에요, squished.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)ㄹ 거예요 = \"my plan / my intention\"</b>. It's not a cold \"will\" — it's what you've decided.\n    When an idol posts \"곧 컴백할 거예요!\" it's a plan and a promise to fans. Pick <b>-ㄹ</b> after a vowel and <b>-을</b> after a consonant.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Formal (교과서) full form</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">갈 것이에요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Correct but stiff — like written English.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Spoken (실제말) short form</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">갈 거예요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">What people actually say — warm and natural.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>거예요 = 것이에요</b>. Say verb stem → pick -ㄹ / -을 → <b>거예요</b>. Put a time word in front — <span class=\"pt-ko\">이번 주말에</span> —\n    and you're making a real plan: <span class=\"pt-ko\">이번 주말에 여행할 거예요</span> (This weekend I'm going to travel).\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌏</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">장소<small>Places · 어디에 가요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_hometown.webp\" alt=\"고향\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('고향')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">고향</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gohyang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hometown</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_city.webp\" alt=\"도시\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('도시')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">도시</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">dosi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">city</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_countryside.webp\" alt=\"시골\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시골')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시골</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">countryside</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 고향이 부산이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 고향이 부산이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">My hometown is Busan.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서울은 큰 도시예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">서울은 큰 도시예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Seoul is a big city.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시골은 조용해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시골은 조용해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The countryside is quiet.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚄</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">여행<small>Travel · 무엇을 타요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_travel.webp\" alt=\"여행\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여행')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">여행</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeohaeng</div><div class=\"vw-en\">trip / travel</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_passport.webp\" alt=\"비행기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('비행기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">비행기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">bihaenggi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">airplane</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_train.webp\" alt=\"기차\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기차')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">기차</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gicha</div><div class=\"vw-en\">train</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('매년 여행을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">매년 여행을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I travel every year.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('비행기를 타고 갈 거예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">비행기를 타고 갈 거예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll go by airplane.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기차가 빨라요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">기차가 빨라요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The train is fast.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">📅</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">계획과 시간<small>Plans & time · 뭘 할 거예요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_plan.webp\" alt=\"계획\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('계획')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">계획</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyehoek</div><div class=\"vw-en\">plan</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_vacation.webp\" alt=\"휴가\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴가')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">휴가</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hyuga</div><div class=\"vw-en\">vacation / holiday</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('휴가 계획을 세워요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">휴가 계획을 세워요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I make vacation plans.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여름 휴가에 고향에 갈 거예요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">여름 휴가에 고향에 갈 거예요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I'll go home for summer vacation.</span></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">✈️ <b>여행 + 자주 쓰는 동사:</b> <b>여행을 하다</b> (do a trip) · <b>고향에 가다</b> (go home) · <b>비행기/기차를 타다</b> (take the plane/train) — pair these words with the verbs you learn this unit to sound natural!</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-1] Reading — 만날 거예요 (-ㄹ/을)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct -(으)ㄹ 거예요 form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">내일 친구를 (　) 거예요. <span class='p-passage'>I will meet my friend tomorrow.</span></div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>만날<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 만나다 ends in ㅏ → add -ㄹ 거예요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>만나을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -을 is only after a consonant</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>만납<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the -ㄹ is missing</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>만나고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -고 나서 means 'after'</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The verb <span class=\"pt-ko\">만나다</span> (to meet) has the stem 만나, which ends in the vowel ㅏ → add <b class=\"hl\">-ㄹ</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">만날 거예요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">만나을</b> wrongly adds 을, <b class=\"hl\">만납</b> loses the -ㄹ, and <b class=\"hl\">만나고</b> is a different pattern (-고 나서 = after).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Rule: vowel stem → -ㄹ 거예요, consonant stem → -을 거예요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-2] Reading — 갈 거예요 (correct sentence)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence is correct?</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">다음 중 맞는 문장을 고르세요. (Choose the correct sentence.)</div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>저는 한국에 갈 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Correct: 가다 + -ㄹ 거예요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>저는 한국에 가을 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no extra 을 after a vowel stem</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 한국에 갈입니다.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 거예요 doesn't become 입니다</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>저는 한국에 가지 거예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ it's 갈 거예요, not 가지</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span> ends in a vowel, so the future form is <span class=\"pt-ko\">갈 거예요</span> — the only correct option.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">가을/갈입니다/가지</b> all break the -(으)ㄹ 거예요 pattern.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 거예요 = 것이에요: <span class=\"pt-ko\">갈 거예요</span> = \"I plan to go.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-3] Reading — 먹기 전에 (-기 전에)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct \"before\" form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">밥을 (　) 전에 손을 씻어요. <span class='p-passage'>I wash my hands before eating.</span></div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>먹을<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -ㄹ 거예요 is future, not 'before'</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>먹고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -고 나서 is 'after'</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>먹기<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 먹다 → 먹기 전에 = before eating</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>먹은<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -은 is not used here</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">-기 전에</span> = \"before doing\". Add -기 to the verb stem: <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다 → 먹기 전에</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">먹을</b> is the future, <b class=\"hl\">먹고</b> is \"after\" (-고 나서), and <b class=\"hl\">먹은</b> is a past form — none fit \"전에\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Sequence: what comes after -기 전에 happens FIRST.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-4] Reading — 하고 나서 (-고 나서)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct \"after\" form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">숙제를 (　) 나서 운동을 해요. <span class='p-passage'>I exercise after doing homework.</span></div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>하기<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -기 전에 is 'before'</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>하고<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 하다 → 하고 나서 = after doing</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>할<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -ㄹ 거예요 is future</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>하면<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -면 is 'if/when'</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">-고 나서</span> = \"after doing\". Add -고 나서 to the verb stem: <span class=\"pt-ko\">하다 → 하고 나서</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">하기</b> belongs with -기 전에, <b class=\"hl\">할</b> is the future, and <b class=\"hl\">하면</b> means \"if\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -고 나서 orders two actions: first 숙제하다, then 운동하다.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-5] Reading — 여행하기 전에 (comprehension)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"나는 한국에 갈 거예요. 여행하기 전에 계획을 세워요. 기차를 타고 도시에 갈 거예요.\" — 여행하기 전에 무엇을 해요?</div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>기차를 타요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that's the trip itself, not before</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>계획을 세워요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ '여행하기 전에 계획을 세워요' = makes a plan first</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>도시에 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that's what he'll do, not before</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>고향에 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ hometown is not in this passage</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The passage says <span class=\"pt-ko\">여행하기 전에 계획을 세워요</span> = before traveling, he <b class=\"hl\">makes a plan</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">기차를 타요 / 도시에 가요</b> are the trip itself; <b class=\"hl\">고향</b> isn't mentioned.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Find -기 전에 — whatever comes right after it is the FIRST action.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-6] Reading — 고향 (vocabulary)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct word.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"저는 서울에 살아요. 그래도 고향은 부산이에요.\" — 부산은 뭐예요? <span class='p-passage'>What is Busan to the speaker?</span></div>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>고향<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 고향 = hometown, where you were born/grew up</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>계획<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 계획 = plan</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>휴가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 휴가 = vacation</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>비행기<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 비행기 = airplane</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker lives in Seoul but was born in Busan — so Busan is his <span class=\"pt-ko\">고향</span> (<b class=\"hl\">hometown</b>).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">계획</b> (plan), <b class=\"hl\">휴가</b> (vacation), and <b class=\"hl\">비행기</b> (airplane) are unrelated.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 고향 is a warm, nostalgic word — \"the place I came from.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-7] Listening — 부산에 갈 거예요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose where they will go.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">내일 부산에 갈 거예요.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('내일 부산에 갈 거예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>부산<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 내일 부산에 갈 거예요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>서울<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ he's going to Busan, not Seoul</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>제주도<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not Jeju</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>고향<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ his hometown is not named here</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">내일 부산에 갈 거예요</span> = tomorrow <b class=\"hl\">(s)he'll go to Busan</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Seoul/Jeju/hometown are not what you heard.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for the place right before <span class=\"pt-ko\">에 갈 거예요</span> — that's the destination.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-8] Listening — 공연하기 전에</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what they do before the performance.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">공연하기 전에 뭐 해요? (What do they do before the performance?)</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('공연하기 전에 노래 연습을 해요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>여행을 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that's not before the performance</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>밥을 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not mentioned</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>노래 연습을 해요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 공연하기 전에 노래 연습을 해요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q8',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>잠을 자요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">공연하기 전에 노래 연습을 해요</span> = before the performance, they <b class=\"hl\">practice singing</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Traveling/eating/sleeping are not what you heard.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -기 전에 signals the action that happens FIRST.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-9] Listening — 콘서트가 끝나고 나서</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what happens after the concert.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">콘서트가 끝나고 나서 뭐 해요? (What happens after the concert ends?)</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('콘서트가 끝나고 나서 팬들과 사진을 찍어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>팬들과 사진을 찍어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ you heard 콘서트가 끝나고 나서 팬들과 사진을 찍어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>바로 집에 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not home right after</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>휴가를 시작해요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not mentioned here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>계획을 세워요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not mentioned here</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">콘서트가 끝나고 나서 팬들과 사진을 찍어요</span> = after the concert, they <b class=\"hl\">take photos with fans</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Going home / vacation / planning are not in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -고 나서 = the SECOND action that follows the first.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[14-10] Listening — 휴가 계획 (summary)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">어떤 계획이에요? (Which is their plan?)</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('휴가 때 고향에 갈 거예요. 도시를 구경하고 나서 시골에서 쉴 거예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n<div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u14q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>City tour, then home<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ wrong order</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Go home, see the city, then rest in the countryside<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ matches 고향 → 도시 → 시골 순서</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Train to the countryside, skip everything<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not what was said</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u14q10',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Vacation at home only<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ they also see the city and countryside</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u14q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">휴가 때 고향에 갈 거예요. 도시를 구경하고 나서 시골에서 쉴 거예요</span> — go home for vacation, <b class=\"hl\">then see the city, then rest in the countryside</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options reverse the order or leave out places.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Combine -(으)ㄹ 거예요 + -고 나서 to tell your whole travel plan in order!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Comeback Plans!</h3>\n    <p>Idols announce comebacks and tour dates with <b>-(으)ㄹ 거예요</b> — a promise to their fans for the next season.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"다음 주에 (　) 거예요!\" — Fill in a plan (컴백/여행/공부/운동) and promise it like an idol's fan-letter!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 15, "title": "Rest well after taking medicine", "en": "약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요", "theme": "health", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 15 · HEALTH</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">15</div><div><h2>Rest Well After Taking Medicine</h2><div class=\"en\">약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요 — Health · -은/ㄴ 후에, -아/어 주세요</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 7/8</span>\n      <h3>채아의 건강 회복 — \"약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요\"</h3>\n      <p>바쁜 스케줄 끝에 보컬 <b>채아</b>가 감기에 걸렸어요. 열이 나고 기침도 나요. 팬들은 채아의 건강이 걱정돼요. 다희가 약을 사 와서 말해요. \"약을 먹은 후에 <b>푹 쉬세요</b>!\" ❤️</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After a busy schedule, vocalist <b>Chaea</b> catches a cold. She has a fever and keeps coughing. Fans worry about Chaea's health. Dahee buys medicine and says, \"약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요!\" (Rest well after taking the medicine!) ❤️</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">❤️ GLOW POINT 7/8 획득 — Health &amp; recovery!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🏥</span> Talk about health &amp; symptoms</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">💊</span> 은/ㄴ 후에 = after doing</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🙏</span> -아/어 주세요 &amp; -아/어서</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 15 — Taking Care of a Sick Member</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🏠 Dorm, after a tiring schedule</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">으, 머리가 아파요. 기침도 나요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Ugh, my head hurts. I keep coughing too.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">어? 열이 있어요! 병원에 가요.</div><div class=\"gl\">What? You have a fever! Let's go to the hospital.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 병원에서 약을 받을게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Okay, I'll get some medicine at the hospital.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬어 주세요. 연습은 우리가 할게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">After you take the medicine, please rest well. We'll do the practice!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">고마워요! 치료받아서 꼭 건강해질게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Thank you! I'll get treated and get healthy for sure.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-은/ㄴ 후에 — \"after doing ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Take the verb stem and add <b>-은 후에</b> (after a final consonant 받침) or <b>-ㄴ 후에</b> (after a vowel), then <b>후에</b> = \"after.\" It shows that one action happens <b>after</b> another!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약을 먹<b>은 후에</b> 푹 쉬세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">After taking medicine, rest well. (먹 has 받침 ㄱ → 은)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">병원에 가<b>ㄴ 후에</b> 약을 받았어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">After going to the hospital, I got medicine. (가 ends in ㅏ → ㄴ)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">점심을 먹은 후에 산책을 해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">After eating lunch, I take a walk.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어 주세요 — \"please do (for me)\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>아/어 주세요</b> to a verb stem to make a <b>polite request</b> — like asking a favor. After a noun alone, <b>주세요</b> just means \"please give me ~.\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">물을 좀 <b>주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please give me some water. (noun + 주세요 = please give)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이 문장을 읽<b>어 주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please read this sentence. (읽다 → 읽어)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">푹 쉬<b>어 주세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Please rest well. (쉬다 → 쉬어)</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어서 — \"so / because\" (reason)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Attach <b>아서/어서</b> to a verb or adjective to give the <b>reason</b>, and the result follows. A bright vowel <b>ㅏ/ㅗ</b> → 아서; otherwise → 어서. One of the most useful endings in everyday Korean!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">감기에 걸리<b>어서</b> 병원에 갔어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I caught a cold, so I went to the hospital.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">열이 있<b>어서</b> 오늘 쉬었어요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I had a fever, so I rested today.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">약을 먹<b>어서</b> 이제 괜찮아요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I took medicine, so I'm fine now.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · \"After doing ~\" — -은/ㄴ 후에</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"After taking the medicine, rest well.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why does <b>먹다</b> suddenly become <b>먹은 후에</b> — and what is that little <b>은</b> doing there?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      To say \"after doing ~\" in English you add a separate word. Korean changes the verb's own tail: take the stem and add <b class=\"hl\">-은 후에</b> (after a final consonant) or <b class=\"hl\">-ㄴ 후에</b> (after a vowel), then <b>후에</b> = \"after.\" The word <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다</span> has the stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹</span>, which ends in the 받침 <b>ㄱ</b> — so it needs <b>은 후에</b>. A vowel-stem verb like <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span> (가) just takes <b>ㄴ 후에</b>: 간 후에. Same 받침 logic as 은/는 and 이에요/예요!\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">약을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">the medicine <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">약 = medicine + object particle 을.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">먹<b>은</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">take (eat) <span class=\"t-sub\">(먹 받침 ㄱ)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">먹 ends in a consonant, so the after-form is <b>먹은</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">후에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">after <span class=\"t-sub\">(time)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">V-은/ㄴ 후에 = \"after doing ~\".</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">푹 쉬세요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">rest well <span class=\"t-sub\">(polite)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">푹 = soundly/deeply · 쉬다 → 쉬어요/쉬세요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요.</b> = \"After taking the medicine, rest well.\" The <b>은/ㄴ</b> depends on the stem's last sound, just like the 받침 rules you already know. Consonant (먹 → ㄱ) grabs <b>은</b>; a vowel (가, 보) grabs <b>ㄴ</b>.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>먹은 후에 — after doing</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">약을 먹<b>은 후에</b> 잤어요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I slept after taking medicine. (one thing after another)</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>먹어서 — so / because</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">약을 먹<b>어서</b> 괜찮아요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Because I took medicine, I'm fine. (reason → result)</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>후에</b> answers \"WHEN?\" → <b>-은/ㄴ 후에</b> (after). <b>-아/어서</b> answers \"WHY?\" → because/so. If the stem has a 받침 use <b>은 후에</b> (먹→먹은), and if it's a vowel use <b>ㄴ 후에</b> (가→간). See it in the title of this whole unit — <b>약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요!</b> 💊\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🤒</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">병과 증상<small>Illness &amp; symptoms · 아파요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_cold.webp\" alt=\"감기\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('감기')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">감기</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gamgi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cold</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_fever2.webp\" alt=\"열\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('열')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">열</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yeol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fever</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_cough.webp\" alt=\"기침\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기침')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">기침</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gichim</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cough</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('감기에 걸렸어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">감기에 걸렸어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I caught a cold.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('열이 있어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">열이 있어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have a fever.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기침이 나요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">기침이 나요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I am coughing.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어디가 아파요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어디가 아파요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Where does it hurt?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🤒 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 감기에 <b>걸리다</b> (걸렸어요) · 열이 <b>있다</b> · 기침이 <b>나다</b> — how Koreans describe being sick!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏥</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">병원과 치료<small>Hospital &amp; treatment</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_hospital.webp\" alt=\"병원\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('병원')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">병원</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">byeongwon</div><div class=\"vw-en\">hospital</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_medicine.webp\" alt=\"약\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">약</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">yak</div><div class=\"vw-en\">medicine</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_treatment.webp\" alt=\"치료\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치료')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">치료</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chiryo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">treatment</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('병원에 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">병원에 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to the hospital.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('약을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">약을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take medicine.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('치료를 받아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">치료를 받아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I get treatment.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('병원에서 진찰을 받았어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">병원에서 진찰을 받았어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I got a check-up at the hospital.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏥 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 병원에 <b>가다</b> · 약을 <b>먹다</b> · 치료를 <b>받다</b> (치료받았어요). Follow the medicine → health path!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💪</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">건강과 회복<small>Health &amp; recovery · 잘 쉬어요</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_health.webp\" alt=\"건강\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('건강')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">건강</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">geongang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">health</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b15_rest.webp\" alt=\"쉬다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쉬다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">쉬다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">swida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to rest</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('건강이 제일 중요해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">건강이 제일 중요해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Health is the most important.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오늘은 푹 쉬었어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오늘은 푹 쉬었어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I rested well today.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('잘 쉬세요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">잘 쉬세요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Rest well!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('몸조심하세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">몸조심하세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Take care of yourself.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💪 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 건강을 <b>챙기다</b> (look after health) · 쉬다 → polite <b>쉬세요</b> (rest). Idol fans say <b>몸조심하세요</b> all the time!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-1 Reading — 받침 → 은 후에]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct \"after ~\" form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">감기에 걸렸어요. 약을 먹(　) 잤어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 은 후에<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 먹 ends in the consonant ㄱ → 은 후에</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 는 후에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 는 needs a word that ends in a vowel</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 을 후에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 을 is the object particle</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 고 후에<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ there is no -고 후에</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹</span> ends in the final consonant <b class=\"hl\">ㄱ</b> (받침), so the after-form is <b class=\"hl\">은 후에</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹은 후에</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">는</b> needs a vowel, <b class=\"hl\">을</b> is the object particle, and -고 후에 does not exist.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 받침(consonant) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">은 후에</span>; vowel → <span class=\"pt-ko\">ㄴ 후에</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-2 Reading — meaning of 후에]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">약을 먹은 후에 쉬었어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I rested <b>after</b> taking the medicine.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 후에 = after → rested after the medicine</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I rested <b>before</b> taking the medicine.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ before would need ~전에</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I took the medicine after resting.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the order is reversed</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I forgot to take the medicine.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ nothing about forgetting</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">-은/ㄴ 후에</span> = <b class=\"hl\">after doing ~</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹은 후에</span> = after taking/eating.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ \"Before\" uses <b class=\"hl\">~전에</b>; the other answers mix up the order or meaning.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">후에</b> (after) ↔ <b class=\"hl\">전에</b> (before) — a classic TOPIK pair!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-3 Reading — vowel stem → ㄴ 후에]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct \"after ~\" form of 보다.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">점심을 (　) 후에 산책을 했어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 보고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 보고 means \"watch and\", not after</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 본<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 보다 ends in the vowel ㅗ → 본 후에</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 보은<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 은 only comes after a consonant</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 보어서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that means \"because I watch\"</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">보다</span> → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">보</span> ends in a vowel, so it takes <b class=\"hl\">ㄴ 후에</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">본 후에</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">보고</b> means \"and then watch\" (V-고), and <b class=\"hl\">보은</b> is impossible after a vowel.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Vowel stem (가, 보) → <b class=\"hl\">ㄴ 후에</b>: 가다 → 간 후에, 보다 → 본 후에!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-4 Reading — -아/어 주세요 (쉬다)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct polite request.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">하준이가 아파요. 팬: \"푹 (　) 주세요!\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 쉬어<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 쉬다 → 쉬어 주세요 = please rest</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 쉬는<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 쉬는 is an adnominal, not a request</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 쉬고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -고 means \"and\", not \"please\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 쉬어서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -어서 gives a reason, not a request</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Polite request = verb stem + <b class=\"hl\">-아/어 주세요</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">쉬다</span> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">쉬어 주세요</span> = \"please rest.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">쉬는/쉬고/쉬어서</b> are different endings — none ask a favor politely.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">-아/어 주세요</b> is how you ask nicely: 쉬어 주세요, 읽어 주세요, 도와주세요!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-5 Reading — meaning of 주세요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">목이 아파요. <span class=\"pt-ko\">물을 좀 주세요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Please give me some water.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ noun + 주세요 = please give me</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Please go get some water yourself.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not about going</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I will give you some water.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 주세요 is a request, not an offer</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>The water is very cold.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no temperature is mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">After a <b class=\"hl\">noun</b>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">주세요</span> simply means <b class=\"hl\">\"please give me ~\"</b>: 물을 좀 주세요.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other answers talk about going, offering, or coldness — not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">N 주세요</b> = please give me N · <b class=\"hl\">V-아/어 주세요</b> = please do ~ for me.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-6 Reading — -아/어서 (reason)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">감기에 걸려서 병원에 갔어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I caught a cold, <b>so</b> I went to the hospital.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ -아/어서 = so/because → reason</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I went to the hospital, then caught a cold.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the cause comes first, not last</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I have a cold but I am fine.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ -어서 connects cause, not contrast</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I rested at home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ she went to the hospital</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">걸리다</span> (감기에 걸리다) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">걸려서</span> = <b class=\"hl\">because (I) caught</b>. So the sentence means \"I caught a cold, so I went to the hospital.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The reason (<b class=\"hl\">-어서</b>) always comes before the result.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">-아/어서</b> = \"because/so\": 감기에 걸려서, 아파서, 바빠서!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-7 Reading — -아/어서 meaning (열)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">열이 있어서 학교에 안 갔어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Because I had a fever, I didn't go to school.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 있어서 = because I had · 안 갔어요 = didn't go</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Because I had a fever, I went to school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 안 갔어요 means did NOT go</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I don't have a fever today.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the fever is the reason</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I really like school.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ nothing about liking school</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">열이 있다</span> = to have a fever → <span class=\"pt-ko\">열이 있어서</span> = <b class=\"hl\">because I had a fever</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">안 갔어요</b> = \"didn't go\", so option 2 is the opposite.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the negation <b class=\"hl\">안</b> — it flips the whole result!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-8 Listening — 약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose the advice you hear.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>  <div class=\"p-q\"><b>What does the speaker tell you to do?</b></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Rest well after taking the medicine.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Go to school right now.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no school is mentioned</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Eat a lot of spicy food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no food suggestion</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Practice the dance all night.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ rest, not practice!</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬세요</span> = <b class=\"hl\">\"rest well after taking the medicine.\"</b></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other answers (school, spicy food, all-night practice) are not in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 In listening, catch the key pattern <b class=\"hl\">~은 후에 … 하세요</b> = \"after ~, please do …\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-9 Listening — 어디가 아파요?]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Listen and choose where it hurts.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('어디가 아파요? 목이 아파요. 기침도 나요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>  <div class=\"p-q\"><b>Where does the person hurt?</b></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>목 (throat)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 목이 아파요 = my throat hurts</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>배 (stomach)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 배 is the stomach, not said</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>머리 (head)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ head is not mentioned</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>다리 (leg)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ leg is not mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio: <span class=\"pt-ko\">어디가 아파요? 목이 아파요. 기침도 나요.</span> — the person has a <b class=\"hl\">목</b> (throat) that hurts.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 배/머리/다리 are other body parts, none of which were said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">~이/가 아파요</b> = \"~ hurts\": 목이 아파요, 머리가 아파요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[15-10 Reading — 건강 (comprehension)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지우는 건강해서 거의 안 아파요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u15q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Jiu is healthy, so he rarely gets sick.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 건강하다 = healthy · 안 아파요 = doesn't hurt/get sick</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Jiu is sick all the time.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 거의 안 = hardly ever</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Jiu went to the hospital today.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no hospital visit is mentioned</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u15q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Jiu doesn't like medicine.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ nothing about disliking medicine</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u15q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">건강하다</span> = to be healthy → <span class=\"pt-ko\">건강해서</span> = <b class=\"hl\">because (he is) healthy</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">거의 안 아파요</span> = rarely gets sick.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">거의 안</b> (hardly ever) means the opposite of \"sick all the time.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">건강해서</b> = healthy + -어서(reason) — you just learned this ending!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Idols' Health Is Everyone's Worry</h3>\n    <p>In K-pop, fans get worried when an idol works too hard and gets sick. On fan sites you'll always see <b>건강이 제일 중요해요!</b> (Health comes first!) and <b>몸조심하세요!</b> (Take care of yourself!). When a group says they're resting, fans cheer — rest is part of the job!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">💜 \"약을 먹은 후에 푹 쉬어 주세요, 채아야! 건강이 제일 중요해요!\" — Write a sweet get-well message to your favorite idol!</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}]}, {"id": 16, "title": "How do I get to Seoul Station?", "en": "여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?", "theme": "directions", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 16 · DIRECTIONS</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">16</div><div><h2>How Do I Get to Seoul Station?</h2><div class=\"en\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요? — Directions · -에서 -까지</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 16 — 오늘은 음악방송 날!</span>\n      <h3>\"여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 <b>음악방송</b> 날! 네 명은 스케줄 장소로 가기 위해 <b>교통</b>을 이용해요. 다희가 지도 앱을 보며 물어요. \"<b>여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?</b>\" 지하철을 타고 빠르게 출발! 🚇</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">It's music-show day! To reach their broadcast schedule, the four members travel by <b>public transport</b>. Dahee checks her map app and asks, \"<b>How do I get to Seoul Station from here?</b>\" They hop on the subway and head off fast! 🚇</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">📍 GLOW POINT 16 — You can ask &amp; answer directions!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  "}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">📍</span> -에서 -까지 (from ~ to ~)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">❓</span> 어떻게 (how)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚇</span> Taking transport to a music show</div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 16 — On the Way to the Music Show</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🚇 At the subway station</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?</div><div class=\"gl\">How do I get to Seoul Station from here?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">지하철로 가요. 1호선을 타요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Take the subway. Ride Line 1.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">지하철역까지 얼마나 걸려요?</div><div class=\"gl\">How long does it take to the subway station?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">집에서 역까지 10분 걸려요. 빨리 가요!</div><div class=\"gl\">It takes 10 minutes from home to the station. Let's go quickly!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-에서 -까지 — from ~ to ~</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Use it to talk about a <b>starting point and an ending point</b>. A에서 B까지 = \"from A to B\". Great for directions and travel time!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">집<b>에서</b> 학교<b>까지</b> 30분 걸려요.</span><span class=\"gl\">It takes 30 minutes from home to school.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">여기<b>에서</b> 서울역<b>까지</b> 어떻게 가요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How do I get to Seoul Station from here?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">서울<b>에서</b> 부산<b>까지</b> 기차로 2시간 반 걸려요.</span><span class=\"gl\">From Seoul to Busan it takes 2 and a half hours by train.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">어떻게 — how?</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The question word for <b>method or way</b>. \"어떻게 가요?\" = \"How do (we) go?\" Put it right before the verb you're asking about.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떻게 가요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How do we go?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어떻게 왔어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">How did you come?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">택시로 가요. 어떻게?</span><span class=\"gl\">We go by taxi. How (about it)?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  "}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어요 — the everyday present polite form</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">The friendly ending for \"I/you/we do ~\" in casual conversation. After ㅏ/ㅗ → <b>-아요</b>, otherwise → <b>-어요</b>; <b>하다</b> → <b>해요</b>. It softens statements into polite talk.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">가<b>다</b> → 가<b>요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">go (가 has ㅏ → -아요 → 가요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">먹<b>다</b> → 먹<b>어요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">eat (먹 has ㅓ → -어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">하<b>다</b> → <b>해요</b></span><span class=\"gl\">do (하다 → 해요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지하철을 타<b>요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I take the subway.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · From Here to There: -에서 -까지 &amp; 어떻게</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"How do I get to Seoul Station from here?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why -에서 -까지 wrap the journey, and how 어떻게 turns it into a question</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      <b class=\"hl\">-에서</b> marks the <b>start</b> (\"from\"), <b class=\"hl\">-까지</b> marks the <b>end</b> (\"to\") — put a place before each, and you've drawn a whole route in two little words: <b class=\"hl\">여기에서</b> (from here) ... <b class=\"hl\">서울역까지</b> (to Seoul Station). Then <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> (\"how\") asks for the <b>method</b>, and <b class=\"hl\">가요</b> is the polite present of 가다 (go). Add the question mark and you're asking for directions exactly like a local.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">여기에서</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">from here <span class=\"t-sub\">(-에서 = start)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">여기 (here)<br>+ 에서 (from)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">서울역까지</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to Seoul Station <span class=\"t-sub\">(-까지 = end)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">서울역 (Seoul St.)<br>+ 까지 (to, as far as)</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어떻게</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">how <span class=\"t-sub\">(method)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Asks \"by what way /<br>by what means?\"</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가요?</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">go <span class=\"t-sub\">(가다 → 가요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Present polite:<br>가 has ㅏ → -아요 → 가요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">A에서 B까지</b> = a route. Answer the \"how\" with a means of transport: <b class=\"t-i-ko\">지하철로 가요</b> (go by subway) uses <b class=\"hl\">로</b> (\"by, via\") — the tool word that rides with 가다. Where <b class=\"hl\">에서</b> starts and <b class=\"hl\">까지</b> ends the journey, <b class=\"hl\">로</b> is the vehicle doing the travelling.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Ask (start → end + how)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">여기<b>에서</b> 서울역<b>까지</b> 어떻게 가요?</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">How do I get from here to Seoul Station?</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Answer (method)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">지하철<b>로</b> 가요.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">I go by subway. 🚇</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <b>에서</b> = \"from\" (start), <b>까지</b> = \"to/as far as\" (end), <b>로</b> = \"by\" (the method), <b>어떻게</b> = \"how\". Put them together and you can ask <i>and</i> answer directions anywhere in Seoul!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚇</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">교통<small>Transport · 서울역/버스/지하철/택시/기차/공항</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">6</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_seoul.webp\" alt=\"서울역\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서울역')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">서울역</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seoul-yeok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">Seoul Station</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_bus.webp\" alt=\"버스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">버스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">beoseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bus</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_subway.webp\" alt=\"지하철\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">지하철</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jihacheol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">subway</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_taxi.webp\" alt=\"택시\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('택시')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">택시</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">taeksi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">taxi</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b14_train.webp\" alt=\"기차\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('기차')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">기차</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gicha</div><div class=\"vw-en\">train</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_airport.webp\" alt=\"공항\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공항')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">공항</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gonghang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">airport</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">How do I get to Seoul Station from here?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스로 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">버스로 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go by bus.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철을 타요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철을 타요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I take the subway.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('공항까지 택시로 갔어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">공항까지 택시로 갔어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I went to the airport by taxi.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚇 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> transport + <b>로/으로</b> = \"by ~\". 버스<b>로</b>, 지하철<b>로</b>, 택시<b>로</b>, 기차<b>로</b>. \"어떻게 가요?\" → \"<b>지하철로</b> 가요!\"</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧭</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">길 & 방향<small>Road & Directions · 길/방향</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_road.webp\" alt=\"길\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('길')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">길</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">road</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_direction.webp\" alt=\"방향\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('방향')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">방향</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">banghyang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">direction</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 이 단어로 자주 쓰는 말</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('길을 건너요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">길을 건너요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I cross the road.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('방향을 알려 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">방향을 알려 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please tell me the direction.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('왼쪽 방향으로 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">왼쪽 방향으로 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go in the left direction.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🧭 <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> <b>길</b> (road) and <b>방향</b> (direction) are the words of asking the way. \"서울역은 <b>어느 방향</b>이에요?\" = Which direction is Seoul Station?</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[1] Reading — Fill in the Blank: -에서 -까지</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct particle.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">집에서 학교(    ) 30분 걸려요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>에서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ start point, not end</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>까지<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ to (school) — end point</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>로<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ by-means</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q1',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>와<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ and/with</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">-에서 -까지</b> = from ~ to ~. <span class=\"pt-ko\">집<b>에서</b></span> (from home) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">학교<b>까지</b></span> (to school). The end point takes <b class=\"hl\">까지</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 에서=from, 로=by, 와=and — none marks the destination.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 First place gets <b class=\"hl\">에서</b> (from), second place gets <b class=\"hl\">까지</b> (to)!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[2] Reading — Meaning: A에서 B까지</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서울에서 부산까지 기차로 2시간 반 걸려요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>From Seoul to Busan it takes 2.5 hours by train.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ from ~ to ~ + by train</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I go to Busan every day.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no habit here</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>The train leaves Seoul at 2:30.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not a time of departure</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Busan is near Seoul.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no distance claim</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">서울<b>에서</b> 부산<b>까지</b></span> = from Seoul to Busan. <b class=\"hl\">기차로</b> = by train, <b class=\"hl\">2시간 반</b> = 2.5 hours.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It talks about the trip time, not habit, departure time, or distance.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Find the two places wrapped by <b class=\"hl\">에서 ... 까지</b> — that is the route!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[3] Reading — Fill in the Blank: 어떻게</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct question word.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">음악방송에(    ) 가요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>어디<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ where (place)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>누가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ who (person)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>어떻게<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ how (by what method)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>뭐<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ what (thing)</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Asking the <b class=\"hl\">way/method</b> to get somewhere → <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> = \"how\". <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게 가요?</span> = How do we go?</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 어디=where, 누가=who, 뭐=what — none asks about method.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> always sits right before the verb: <b class=\"hl\">어떻게 가요?</b></div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[4] Reading — Meaning: 어떻게</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct question.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>When does the train leave?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no time word</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>Where is Seoul Station?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ place is given: 서울역까지</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>How do I get to Seoul Station from here?<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ asks the way</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Why are you going?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no reason</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">여기에서</b> = from here, <b class=\"hl\">서울역까지</b> = to Seoul Station, <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> = how. So: \"How do I get to Seoul Station from here?\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It never asks time, location (서울역 is the target), or reason.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Route (<b class=\"hl\">에서 ... 까지</b>) + <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> = a directions question!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[5] Reading — -아/어요 Conjugation (가다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct present polite form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">지하철을(    ).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>타요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ take (타 has ㅏ → -아요 → 타요)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>타<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ plain stem</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>탔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ past</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>탈 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">타다</span> (to ride) → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">타</span> ends in ㅏ → + <b class=\"hl\">-아요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">타요</span>. \"I take the subway.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 타=plain, 탔어요=past, 탈 거예요=future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Bright vowel <b class=\"hl\">ㅏ/ㅗ</b> takes <b class=\"hl\">-아요</b>: 타<b>요</b>, 가<b>요</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[6] Listening — 어떻게 가요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best reply.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('음악방송에 어떻게 가요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">음악방송에 어떻게 가요?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>지하철로 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ by subway (how/method)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>지하철역이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ that is a place, not a method</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>네, 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ yes, went (past)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>서울역이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ a station, not how</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Question <span class=\"pt-ko\">어떻게 가요?</span> asks <b class=\"hl\">how</b> → the answer names the transport: <span class=\"pt-ko\">지하철<b>로</b> 가요</span> (go by subway).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others answer \"where\" or \"did you go?\" instead of \"how\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Answer <b class=\"hl\">어떻게</b> with transport + <b class=\"hl\">로</b>: 버스로, 지하철로, 택시로!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[7] Reading — Meaning: -에서 -까지</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the correct meaning.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">집에서 공항까지 택시로 갔어요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I went from home to the airport by taxi.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ from home to airport + by taxi</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>The airport is near my home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no distance claim</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I took a taxi inside the airport.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ the taxi went to the airport</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>I will go to the airport.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ past tense 갔어요</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">집<b>에서</b> 공항<b>까지</b></span> = from home to the airport. <b class=\"hl\">택시로</b> = by taxi, <b class=\"hl\">갔어요</b> = went (past).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ It states a route and a past trip, not distance or the future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Past <b class=\"hl\">-았/었어요</b> + route <b class=\"hl\">에서 ... 까지</b> = \"went from ~ to ~\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[8] Reading — Transport Vocab</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct transport.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\">공항에 어떻게 가요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>기차로 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ trains link cities, not an airport shuttle trip</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>지하철로 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ possible, but not the best fit for 공항</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>버스로 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ too general</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>공항버스로 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ airport bus to the airport</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question targets the <b class=\"hl\">공항</b> (airport). The clearest answer is <b class=\"hl\">공항버스</b> (airport limousine bus) — the word 공항 appears right in the matching option.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 기차/지하철/버스 are transport, but only 공항버스 is the airport shuttle.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Match the transport to the destination: 공항 → 공항버스, 서울역 → 지하철!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[9] Reading — -아/어요 Conjugation (먹다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct present polite form.</div>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">아침을(    ).</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>먹다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ dictionary form</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ eat (먹 has ㅓ → -어요)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>먹었어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ past</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>먹을 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ future</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">먹다</span> → stem <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹</span> ends in the dark vowel ㅓ → + <b class=\"hl\">-어요</b> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹어요</span>. \"I eat breakfast.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 먹다=plain, 먹었어요=past, 먹을 거예요=future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Non-bright vowels (ㅓ/ㅜ/ㅣ) take <b class=\"hl\">-어요</b>: 먹<b>어요</b>!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[10] Listening — How to Get to Seoul Station</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요? 지하철로 가요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">여기에서 서울역까지 어떻게 가요? 지하철로 가요.</span></div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u16q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>지하철로 서울역까지 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ subway to Seoul Station</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>버스로 공항까지 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ bus to airport — wrong</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>택시로 집까지 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ taxi home — wrong</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u16q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>기차로 부산까지 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ train to Busan — wrong</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u16q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard the route <span class=\"pt-ko\">서울역<b>까지</b></span> and the method <span class=\"pt-ko\">지하철<b>로</b></span>. The trip: <b class=\"hl\">by subway to Seoul Station</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ All others swap in a different transport or destination (공항/집/부산).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Catch the <b class=\"hl\">destination</b> (까지) and the <b class=\"hl\">method</b> (로) — together they answer \"how to get there!\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Getting to the Music Show</h3>\n    <p>Idols film <b>music shows</b> at broadcast stations around Seoul. Fans take the <b>subway</b> to catch the \"출근길\" (commute) photos — from home, Seoul Station, and even the airport, they ask and answer directions just like you just learned!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🚇 인기가요(SBS)는 상암, 뮤직뱅크(KBS)는 여의도, 음악중심(MBC)은 일산. 어느 방향으로 가요? \"지하철로 갑시다!\" — Try asking the way in Korean at your next fan meeting!</div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>"}]}, {"id": 17, "title": "What should I bring to the housewarming?", "en": "집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?", "theme": "obligation", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 17 · OBLIGATION — 집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">17</div><div><h2>What should I bring to the housewarming?</h2><div class=\"en\">집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요? — Obligation with -아/어야 돼요</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">🏠 GLOWSIS STORY · 17 — New Apartment Party</span>\n      <h3>채아의 새집 — \"집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?\"</h3>\n      <p>리더 <b>채아</b>가 새집으로 <b>이사</b>했어요. 멤버들을 <b>집들이</b>에 <b>초대</b>했어요. 다들 \"<b>선물</b>을 뭘 사 가야 돼요?\" 하며 고민해요. <b>꽃</b>을 살까, <b>케이크</b>를 살까? 🎁</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Leader <b>Chaea</b> moved into a new apartment (<b>이사</b>). She <b>invited</b> (<b>초대</b>) the members to a <b>housewarming</b> party (<b>집들이</b>). Everyone worries, \"What <b>gift</b> (<b>선물</b>) should we go buy and bring?\" Flowers (<b>꽃</b>) or a cake (<b>케이크</b>)? 🎁</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🏠 GLOW POINT 17 — Say what you must do with -아/어야 돼요!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">✅</span> Say you must: -아/어야 돼요</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👜</span> Take/bring: 가지고 가다/오다</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎁</span> Ask what: 뭘</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 17 — Choosing a Housewarming Gift</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🎁 Gift shop</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">이번 주말에 제 새집 집들이에 초대할게요!</div><div class=\"gl\">I will invite you all to my new-apartment housewarming this weekend!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">와, 좋아요! 그런데 집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Wow, great! But what should we go buy and bring to the housewarming?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">집들이에는 꼭 선물을 사 가야 돼요. 꽃이 좋아요?</div><div class=\"gl\">For a housewarming you really must go buy a gift. Is a flower good?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">꽃도 좋지만 케이크를 사 가지고 가요. 같이 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Flowers are nice, but let us buy and take a cake along. We will eat it together!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저는 과일하고 음료를 사 가지고 갈게요.</div><div class=\"gl\">OK! I will go buy fruit and drinks and bring them along.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-아/어야 돼요 — \"must / have to\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>아야 돼요</b> (stem vowel ㅏ/ㅗ) or <b>어야 돼요</b> (any other vowel) to a verb stem to say \"must, have to\". <b>하다</b> becomes <b>해야 돼요</b>. In <b>사 가야 돼요</b> the polite <b>돼요</b> = \"it has to be done\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">선물을 사야 <b>돼요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I have to buy a gift.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">이사해서 일찍 가야 <b>돼요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I must go early for the move.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">밥을 먹어야 <b>돼요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I have to eat.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">가지고 가다 / 가지고 오다 — \"take / bring\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>가지고</b> = \"carrying / holding\". Pair it with <b>가다</b> (go) to <b>take</b> something along, or <b>오다</b> (come) to <b>bring</b> it here. <b>사 가지고 가요</b> = \"buy it and take it along\".</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">케이크를 사 <b>가지고 가요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Let us buy a cake and take it along.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">꽃을 <b>가지고 왔어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I brought flowers (came carrying them).</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">음료를 <b>가지고 올게요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I will bring drinks along.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">뭘 — \"what\" (object)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>뭘</b> = <b>뭐</b> (what) + the object particle <b>를</b>, squashed together. Use it right before a verb to ask WHAT you do: <b>뭘 사 가야 돼요?</b> = \"what do I have to buy and bring?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>뭘</b> 사 가야 돼요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What do I have to buy and bring?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>뭘</b> 먹고 싶어요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What do you want to eat?</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\"><b>뭘</b> 좋아해요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What do you like?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · \"집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"What do I have to buy and bring to the housewarming?\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">English says \"I have to\" as two separate words. How does Korean pack obligation into ONE ending — and why does the sentence have two verbs 사 + 가?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Korean marks obligation at the END of the verb, not with a helper word at the front. You take a verb like\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> (to buy), and because the thing must <b>go with you to another place</b>, you first link it to <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span>: <b>사 가다</b> = \"buy and (go) bring\". Then obligation rides on the last verb\n      <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span> → <span class=\"pt-ko\">가야 돼요</span> = \"must (go)\". So <span class=\"pt-ko\">사 가야 돼요</span> literally = \"[I] must go buy and bring\".\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">집들이에</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">to the housewarming <span class=\"t-sub\">(place + 에)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">집들이 = the housewarming party (a noun). Add <b>에</b> = \"to\" the place.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">뭘</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">what <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">뭐 (what) + 를 (object marker) → <b>뭘</b>. It asks WHAT, right before the action verb.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">사 가야 돼요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">must go buy &amp; bring <span class=\"t-sub\">(obligation)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">사다 → 사 가다. 가다 ends in ㅏ → <b>가야 돼요</b> (must). Everything rides on that final -아야 돼요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-아/어야 돼요 = \"must\"</b> — attach to a verb stem: <b>사야 돼요</b> (사다), <b>가야 돼요</b> (가다), <b>먹어야 돼요</b> (먹다), <b>해야 돼요</b> (하다). Same vowel harmony you already know: ㅏ/ㅗ → <b>-아야</b>, anything else → <b>-어야</b>.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>ㅏ/ㅗ vowel → -아야 돼요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">꽃을 사<b>야 돼요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">사다 (buy) → 사야 돼요 → \"I must buy flowers.\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Other vowel / 하다 → -어야 돼요</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">밥을 먹<b>어야 돼요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">먹다 (eat) → 먹어야 돼요 → \"I have to eat.\" 하다 → 해야 돼요.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> <span class=\"pt-ko\">돼요</span> is short for <span class=\"pt-ko\">되어요</span> = \"it becomes (done)\". So <b>사야 돼요</b> feels like \"buying becomes (necessary)\" — that is how Korean says \"have to\". And add <b>가지고 가다/오다</b> when the thing moves WITH you: <span class=\"pt-ko\">케이크를 사 가지고 가요</span> = buy it and take it along!\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🏠</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">이사와 집들이<small>Moving &amp; housewarming · 새집 파티</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_housewarming.webp\" alt=\"집들이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집들이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">집들이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jipdeuri</div><div class=\"vw-en\">housewarming party</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_moving.webp\" alt=\"이사\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이사')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">이사</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">isa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">moving (to a new home)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_invitation.webp\" alt=\"초대\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('초대')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">초대</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">chodae</div><div class=\"vw-en\">invitation</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('채아 씨가 새집으로 이사했어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">채아 씨가 새집으로 이사했어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Chaea moved into a new apartment.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이번 주말에 집들이를 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이번 주말에 집들이를 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We are having a housewarming this weekend.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집들이에 초대해 주세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">집들이에 초대해 주세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Please invite me to the housewarming.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🏠 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 이사하다 (to move) → 새집 (new house) → people <b>집들이</b>에 <b>초대</b>하다. A 집들이 is the party after an 이사.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🎁</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">사 가지고 가는 것<small>Gifts to bring · 뭘 사 가요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_gift.webp\" alt=\"선물\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('선물')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">선물</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seonmul</div><div class=\"vw-en\">gift / present</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_flower.webp\" alt=\"꽃\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('꽃')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">꽃</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">kkot</div><div class=\"vw-en\">flower</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_cake.webp\" alt=\"케이크\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('케이크')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">케이크</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">keikeu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">cake</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('집들이에는 선물을 사 가야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">집들이에는 선물을 사 가야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">You have to buy and bring a gift to a housewarming.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('꽃을 사 가지고 갈게요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">꽃을 사 가지고 갈게요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I will buy flowers and take them along.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('케이크를 사 갈까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">케이크를 사 갈까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we go buy a cake?</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🎁 <b>선물 선택:</b> As a housewarming gift people often buy and bring <b>꽃</b>, <b>케이크</b>, or tissues (휴지). Say <b>사 가지고 가요</b> = \"buy and take along\".</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🍎</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">먹고 마셔요<small>Food &amp; drink for the party</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u6_fruit.webp\" alt=\"과일\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('과일')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">과일</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gwail</div><div class=\"vw-en\">fruit</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b17_drink.webp\" alt=\"음료\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음료')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음료</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumnyo</div><div class=\"vw-en\">drink / beverage</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you will hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('과일하고 음료를 사 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">과일하고 음료를 사 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let us buy fruit and drinks and take them.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음료를 많이 가지고 가야 돼요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">음료를 많이 가지고 가야 돼요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We have to bring a lot of drinks.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🍎 <b>손님 = bring food:</b> At a Korean 집들이, guests often <b>사 가지고 와요</b> — buy fruit (과일) and drinks (음료) and bring them to share!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-1] Reading — Fill in the blank</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form of <b>-아/어야 돼요</b> (must).</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-q\">집들이에 선물을 꼭 (    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>사야 돼요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ have to buy — 사다</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>사고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ want to buy</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>샀어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ bought, past</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>살 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ will buy, future</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">We must buy a gift, so we need the obligation ending <b class=\"hl\">-아/어야 돼요</b>. <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> ends in ㅏ → <span class=\"pt-ko\">사야 돼요</span> = \"have to buy\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 사고 싶어요=want, 샀어요=past, 살 거예요=future — none means \"must\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grammar 1: stem + <b class=\"hl\">아야 돼요</b> (ㅏ/ㅗ) or <b class=\"hl\">어야 돼요</b> (other) = \"have to\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-2] Reading — Fill in the blank (하다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form of <b>하다</b> + <b>-아/어야 돼요</b>.</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-q\">저는 오늘 공부(    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>해야 돼요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ have to do — 하다</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>하고 싶어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ want to do</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>했어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ did, past</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>할 거예요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ will do, future</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">It is a must, so use the obligation ending. <span class=\"pt-ko\">하다</span> (to do) → <b class=\"hl\">해야 돼요</b> = \"have to do\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 하고 싶어요=want, 했어요=past, 할 거예요=future.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">하다</span> is special: 하 + 여야 → <b class=\"hl\">해야 돼요</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-3] Listening — What must we bring?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what they must buy and bring.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요? 케이크를 사 가야 돼요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>과일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ not heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>케이크<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ cake — heard</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>음료만<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ only drinks</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q3',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>꽃<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ flowers not said</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">케이크를 사 가야 돼요</span> — they must go buy and bring a <b class=\"hl\">케이크</b> (cake).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 과일/음료/꽃 were not mentioned as the thing to bring.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <b class=\"hl\">뭘</b> + <b class=\"hl\">사 가야 돼요</b> — \"what do we have to buy and bring?\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-4] Reading — 뭘 meaning</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">What does <b>뭘</b> mean in this question?</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-q\">뭘 사 가야 돼요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>Where<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ place word</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>What<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ object what — 뭐 + 를</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>Who<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ person word</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>When<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ time word</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">뭘</span> = <span class=\"pt-ko\">뭐</span> (what) + the object particle <b class=\"hl\">를</b>, merged. It asks WHAT is the object of the verb.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Where/Who/When are different question words (어디/누구/언제).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grammar 3: <span class=\"pt-ko\">뭘 사 가야 돼요?</span> = \"What do I have to buy and bring?\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-5] Reading — Meaning of the sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the closest meaning of this sentence.</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-q\">꽃을 사 가야 돼요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>I must buy flowers and bring them.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ buy + take along</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>I bought flowers yesterday.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ past, not about bringing</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>I do not like flowers.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ no dislike here</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>Flowers are cheap.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ not about price</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">꽃을 사 가야 돼요</span> = buy flowers and <b class=\"hl\">take them along</b> (사 + 가다) — \"I must go buy flowers and bring them.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others add past tense, dislike, or price that are not in the sentence.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grammar 1 + 2 together: <span class=\"pt-ko\">사 가야 돼요</span> = \"must buy and (go) bring\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-6] Reading — 가지고 가다/오다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct particle verb (take vs bring).</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-q\">파티에 선물을 (    ).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>가지고 가요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ take it (away) with me</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>가지고 왔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ brought it here</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>갔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ went alone</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>왔어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ came alone</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You are going TO the party, so the gift moves <b>with you away</b>: <b class=\"hl\">가지고 가요</b> = \"take it along\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 가지고 왔어요 = brought it here (toward the speaker).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grammar 2: <b class=\"hl\">가지고 가다</b> = take (go with it), <b class=\"hl\">가지고 오다</b> = bring (come with it).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-7] Listening — Choose what you hear</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the sentence you hear.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('음료를 가지고 왔어요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>음료를 가지고 왔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ brought drinks (came with)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>음료를 가지고 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ take drinks (go)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>음료를 사 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ go buy drinks</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>음료가 없어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ there are no drinks</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">음료를 가지고 왔어요</span> — \"I <b class=\"hl\">brought</b> drinks (came carrying them)\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 가지고 가요 = take (go), 사 가요 = go buy, 없어요 = not exist.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 The key sound is <b class=\"hl\">왔어요</b> (came) vs <b class=\"hl\">가요</b> (go).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-8] Reading — Choosing the right gift word</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which word matches the picture meaning <b>cake</b>?</div>\n\n\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>과일<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ fruit</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>케이크<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ cake</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>꽃<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ flower</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q8',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>선물<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ gift</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">케이크</span> = <b class=\"hl\">cake</b>, a sweet dessert people often bring to a housewarming to share.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 과일=fruit, 꽃=flower, 선물=gift.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 All four are housewarming gifts — the picture shows a <b class=\"hl\">cake</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-9] Listening — Where must they go?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what you must do today.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 집들이에 가야 돼요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>밥을 먹어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ not the must</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>영화를 봐요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ not said</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>집들이에 가야 돼요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ must go to the housewarming</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>집에서 자요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ opposite</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">You heard <span class=\"pt-ko\">오늘 집들이에 가야 돼요</span> — today I <b class=\"hl\">must go</b> to the housewarming.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Eating, a movie, and sleeping were not said as the plan.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for <b class=\"hl\">가야 돼요</b> (가다 + 아야 돼요) = \"must go\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[17-10] Listening — Best reply</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen to the question and choose the best reply.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('집들이에 뭘 사 가지고 가야 돼요?')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u17q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span>꽃을 사 가지고 갈게요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ I will buy flowers and take them</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span>네, 맛있어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ not about food here</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span>저는 학생이에요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ unrelated</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u17q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span>어제 갔어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ past, wrong time</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u17q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The question <span class=\"pt-ko\">집들이에 뭘 사 가야 돼요?</span> asks WHAT to buy and bring → answer with the thing: <span class=\"pt-ko\">꽃을 사 가지고 갈게요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others do not answer \"what should I bring\".</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Reply pattern: (thing) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">을/를 사 가지고 갈게요</span> = \"I will buy ~ and take it along\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Housewarming Gift Etiquette</h3>\n    <p>In Korea, when someone has a <b>집들이</b> (housewarming), guests always bring a <b>선물</b> — never arrive empty-handed. Idols follow this rule, too!</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🎁 Bring something useful for the new home: 꽃 (flowers), 케이크 (cake), or even 휴지 (tissues) — a lucky, practical gift. Say \"집들이 축하해요!\" (Congratulations on the housewarming!)</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 18, "title": "It's congested so let's take the subway", "en": "길이 막히니까 지하철로 갑시다", "theme": "strong suggestion", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 18 · GETTING THERE ON TIME</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">18</div><div><h2>It's Congested, So Let's Take the Subway</h2><div class=\"en\">길이 막히니까 지하철로 갑시다 — Reasons · -(으)니까 / Let's · -(으)ㅂ시다</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · LET'S GO</span>\n      <h3>콘서트에 늦을 것 같아 — \"지하철로 갑시다!\"</h3>\n      <p>오늘은 팬들이 기다리는 <b>콘서트</b> 날이에요! 그런데 차가 많아서 <b>길이 막혀요</b>. 아란이 말해요. \"시간이 없으니까 지하철로 <b>갑시다</b>!\" 다들 빨리 서둘러요. 🚇</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">Today is the <b>concert</b> fans have been waiting for! But there are so many cars that the <b>road is blocked</b>. Aran says, \"Since we have no time, <b>let's go</b> by subway!\" Everyone hurries up. 🚇</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 18/20 획득 — Let's go together!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚇</span> Suggest going somewhere (갑시다)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🚗</span> Give a reason (-(으)니까)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">⏱️</span> Traffic & time vocabulary</div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 18 — On Our Way to the Concert</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🚇 Outside the concert venue</span>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">콘서트가 7시예요. 지금 몇 시예요?</div><div class=\"gl\">The concert is at 7. What time is it now?</div></div>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">벌써 6시 반이에요. 차가 너무 많아요.</div><div class=\"gl\">It's already 6:30. There are so many cars.</div></div>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">길이 막히니까 지하철로 갑시다!</div><div class=\"gl\">The road is blocked, so let's go by subway!</div></div>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 그런데 버스는 안 막혀요?</div><div class=\"gl\">Good! But isn't the bus blocked?</div></div>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">버스도 막혀요. 시간이 없으니까 빨리 서두릅시다!</div><div class=\"gl\">The bus is blocked too. Since we have no time, let's hurry!</div></div>\n    </div>\n<div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">네, 지하철이 제일 빨라요. 같이 갑시다!</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes, the subway is fastest. Let's go together!</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)니까 — Because / Reason</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>-(으)니까</b> after a verb or adjective to say <b>\"because / so\"</b>. After a vowel use <b>-니까</b>, after a final consonant use <b>-으니까</b>. The reason comes first!</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">길이 막히<b>니까</b> 지하철로 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">막히 (no final consonant) → 니까: \"The road is blocked, so we go by subway.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">시간이 없<b>으니까</b> 빨리 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">없 ends in ㅆ → 으니까: \"Since there is no time, we go fast.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">재미있으니까 같이 가자!</span><span class=\"gl\">\"It's fun, so let's go together!\"</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-(으)ㅂ시다 — Let's (formal suggestion)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Use <b>-(으)ㅂ시다</b> to make a strong, polite suggestion — <b>\"let's do it!\"</b> After a vowel use <b>-ㅂ시다</b>, after a consonant use <b>-읍시다</b>. Great for rallying the group.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지하철로 갑<b>시다</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">가 ends in a vowel (ㅏ) → ㅂ시다: \"Let's take the subway.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 먹읍<b>시다</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">먹 ends in ㄱ → 읍시다: \"Let's eat together.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">빨리 서두릅시다.</span><span class=\"gl\">\"Let's hurry up.\"</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-지 않다 — Not (negative)</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put <b>-지 않다</b> after a verb or adjective stem to make it negative — <b>\"not ~\"</b>. It is the longer, softer cousin of <b>안</b>. Use it to say a road is <b>not</b> blocked.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">지금은 길이 막히<b>지 않아요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">\"The road is not blocked right now.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">버스가 느리<b>지 않아요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">\"The bus is not slow.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">늦지 않게 서둘러요.</span><span class=\"gl\">\"Hurry so you won't be late.\"</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"지하철로 갑시다\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">지하철로 갑시다.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Let's take the subway.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why does a K-POP manager shout <b>\"갑시다!\"</b> to get everyone moving — and what is the <b>-로</b> doing there?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      When you need to move the whole team, Korean doesn't say \"let us go\" word by word. Take the verb stem\n      <b>가</b> (from <span class=\"pt-ko\">가다</span>, to go) and add the strong, polite suggestion ending <b>-(으)ㅂ시다</b>:\n      <b>갑시다</b> = \"let's go!\" Add <b>-로</b> (= \"by way of / by means of\") after a vehicle and you get\n      <b>지하철로</b> (by subway) — so <b>지하철로 갑시다</b> = \"let's go by subway.\" In K-POP, <b>갑시다!</b>\n      is how a leader marches the whole team toward the stage or the van.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">지하철<b>로</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">by subway <span class=\"t-sub\">(means)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">지하철 = subway. Add <b>-로</b> to say \"by ~\" — the transport you use.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">가<b>ㅂ시다</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">let's go <span class=\"t-sub\">(suggestion)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">가다 stem 가 ends in a vowel → attach <b>ㅂ시다</b>: <b>갑시다</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">…니까</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">because <span class=\"t-sub\">(reason)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">Give your reason first: <b>길이 막히니까</b> = \"because the road is blocked.\"</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">-(으)니까 = \"because / so\"</b> — glue it to the end of the first clause to give your reason.\n    Vowel stem (막히<b>니까</b>) → 니까; consonant stem (없<b>으니까</b>) → 으니까. Then comes the result:\n    <span class=\"pt-ko\">길이 막히니까 지하철로 갑시다</span> — reason + suggestion in one sentence.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Vowel stem → -니까 / -ㅂ시다</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">가<b>니까</b> · 가<b>ㅂ시다</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">가·오·마시 → \"so / let's\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Consonant stem → -으니까 / -읍시다</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">없<b>으니까</b> · 먹<b>읍시다</b></span><br><span class=\"t-en\">없·먹·받 → \"so / let's\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> the SAME 받침 rule runs through both endings. Consonant → <b>으니까 / 읍시다</b>, vowel →\n    <b>니까 / ㅂ시다</b>. Say \"no\" politely with <b>-지 않다</b> instead of 안: <span class=\"pt-ko\">막히지 않아요</span> = \"it's not blocked.\"\n    Now give a reason and rally the team: <span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 없으니까 빨리 갑시다!</span> 🏃‍💨\n  </div>\n</div>\n"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🚗</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">길과 교통<small>Roads & traffic · 어떻게 가요?</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">5</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b16_road.webp\" alt=\"길\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('길')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">길</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gil</div><div class=\"vw-en\">road</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_blocked.webp\" alt=\"막히다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('막히다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">막히다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">makhida</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to be blocked</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_traffic.webp\" alt=\"교통\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('교통')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">교통</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gyotong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">traffic</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_subway.webp\" alt=\"지하철\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">지하철</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">jihacheol</div><div class=\"vw-en\">subway</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u7_bus.webp\" alt=\"버스\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">버스</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">beoseu</div><div class=\"vw-en\">bus</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('길이 막혀요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">길이 막혀요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The road is blocked.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('교통이 많아요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">교통이 많아요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There is a lot of traffic.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철로 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철로 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go by subway.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('버스로 갑시다.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">버스로 갑시다.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's take the bus.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('지하철이 버스보다 빨라요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">지하철이 버스보다 빨라요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">The subway is faster than the bus.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🚗 <b>막히다 · 길 · 교통:</b> 길 = the road, 교통 = the traffic on it, and 막히다 = \"to be blocked / stuck\". In K-POP, the vans sit in <b>교통 체증</b> (traffic jam), so the team rushes to the <b>지하철</b> instead!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">⏰</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">시간과 서두르기<small>Time & hurrying · 늦지 않게!</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">3</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_time.webp\" alt=\"시간\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시간</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sigan</div><div class=\"vw-en\">time</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_quickly.webp\" alt=\"빨리\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('빨리')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">빨리</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ppalli</div><div class=\"vw-en\">quickly</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b18_hurry.webp\" alt=\"서두르다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서두르다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">서두르다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">seodureuda</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to hurry</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간이 없어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시간이 없어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">There is no time.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('빨리 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">빨리 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Go quickly.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('서두릅시다!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">서두릅시다!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Let's hurry!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시간이 있으니까 천천히 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시간이 있으니까 천천히 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Since there is time, go slowly.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('늦지 않게 서둘러요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">늦지 않게 서둘러요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Hurry so you won't be late.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">⏰ <b>시간 · 빨리 · 서두르다:</b> 시간 = time, 빨리 = \"quickly\", and 서두르다 = \"to hurry\". When the show starts soon, an idol shouts <b>\"빨리! 서두르자!\"</b> — hurry, let's go!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-1] Reading — 길이 막히니까</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">왜 지하철로 가요? — 버스는 너무 느려요. (　) 지하철이 더 빨라요. Choose the best reason.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 길이 막히니까<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 막히 + 니까 = \"because the road is blocked\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 길이 안 막히니까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 안 막히 = NOT blocked → wrong reason</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 시간이 많으니까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 많 = lots of time → would NOT rush</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 버스가 빠르니까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ fast bus → wouldn't switch to subway</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker wants the subway because the <b class=\"hl\">road is blocked</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">막히</span> + <b class=\"hl\">-니까</b> = <span class=\"pt-ko\">막히니까</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">안 막히니까</b> (\"not blocked\") and <b class=\"hl\">시간이 많으니까</b> (\"lots of time\") are the wrong reasons to hurry.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Vowel stem 막히 → <b class=\"hl\">-니까</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-2] Reading — 갑시다 / 읍시다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">선생님이 말해요: \"자, 이제 (　).\" Choose the correct \"let's go\" form.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 갑시다<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 가 (vowel ㅏ) → ㅂ시다: \"let's go\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 가읍시다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 가 is a vowel stem → never 읍시다</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 갑니다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 니다 = plain polite statement (\"goes\")</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가지 않다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 지 않다 = \"not go\" (negative)</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><b class=\"hl\">가다</b> ends in the vowel ㅏ, so the suggestion is <b class=\"hl\">가 + ㅂ시다</b> = <span class=\"pt-ko\">갑시다</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">읍시다</b> is only for consonant stems like 먹<b class=\"hl\">읍시다</b>; 갑니다 is a plain statement, and 가지 않다 is negative.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Vowel → <b class=\"hl\">-ㅂ시다</b>, consonant → <b class=\"hl\">-읍시다</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-3] Reading — 교통</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">차가 아주 많아요. 오늘 (　)이 정말 많아요. There are so many cars today.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 길<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 길 = the road itself</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 시간<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 시간 = time</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 교통<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 교통 = the traffic (all the cars)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q3',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 버스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 버스 = the bus</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">\"차가 많아요\" = many cars → the situation is heavy <b class=\"hl\">traffic</b>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">교통</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 길 is the road, 시간 is time, and 버스 is one vehicle.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">교통이 많다</span> = there is a lot of traffic.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-4] Reading — -(으)니까 reason</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">\"시간이 없으니까 택시를 탑시다.\" What is the reason?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 시간이 있어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 있 = have time → opposite</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 시간이 없어요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 없 + 으니까 = \"since there is no time\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 택시가 비싸요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ expensive → wouldn't take it</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q4',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 버스가 빨라요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ bus is fast → unrelated</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The sentence uses <span class=\"pt-ko\">없<b class=\"hl\">으니까</b></span> = \"because there is <b class=\"hl\">no time</b>.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 없 ends in ㅆ (consonant) → <b class=\"hl\">-으니까</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 The clause BEFORE 니까 is always the reason.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-5] Listening — 지하철이 빨라요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('지금 버스가 막혀요. 그래서 지하철로 갑니다.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What is the speaker choosing?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 지하철<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 막힌 버스 대신 지하철로 = \"by subway\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 버스<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 버스는 막혀 있어요 = it is blocked</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 택시<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 택시 isn't mentioned</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 기차<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 기차 isn't mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">버스가 막혀요</span> (bus is blocked), so they go <b class=\"hl\">지하철로</b> (by subway).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The bus is the problem, not the choice.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 막히다 = \"to be blocked\"; hear it and switch vehicles!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-6] Reading — -(으)ㅂ시다 context</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">콘서트에 늦을 것 같아요. (　) Choose the best suggestion.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 천천히 갑시다.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 천천히 = slowly → would make us later</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 빨리 서두릅시다.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 서두르다 → \"let's hurry up\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 길에서 잡시다.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ stop on the road → wrong</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q6',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 집에 갑시다.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ go home → missing the concert</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Running late means you must <b class=\"hl\">hurry</b>. 서두르다 stem = 서두르; the ㅡ is dropped and <b>ㅂ시다</b> attaches → <span class=\"pt-ko\">서두릅시다</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Going slowly or home is the opposite of being on time.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <span class=\"pt-ko\">빨리 서두릅시다!</span> = \"let's hurry up quickly!\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-7] Reading — -지 않다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">지금은 차가 없어요. 그래서 길이 (　).</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 막혀요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 막혀 = IS blocked → opposite</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 막히지 않아요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 막히 + 지 않다 = \"not blocked\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 막힙시다<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ㅂ시다 = \"let's be blocked\" → no meaning</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 막히니까<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 니까 = \"because blocked\"</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">No cars now → the road <b class=\"hl\">is not blocked</b>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">막히<b class=\"hl\">지 않아요</b></span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 막혀요 = it IS blocked; the others don't make a \"not\" here.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">-지 않다</b> is the polite negative; 안 is the short form.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-8] Listening — 늦지 않게</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('우리 늦지 않게 빨리 가요!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">What does the speaker want to avoid?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 늦는 것<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 늦지 않게 = \"so we DON'T be late\"</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 지하철 타는 것<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not about taking the subway</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 집에 가는 것<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not about going home</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 차 타는 것<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ not about riding a car</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">늦<b class=\"hl\">지 않게</b></span> = \"so that we are <b class=\"hl\">not late</b>\". The goal is avoiding being late.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other options name things not said in the audio.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 -지 않게 = \"-지 않다\" + 게 = \"so as not to ~\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-9] Reading — 시간이 없어요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">시간이 없으니까 빨리 가요. What is the speaker saying?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> We have lots of time, so go slowly.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 있으면 천천히 — but he says 없으니까</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Because there is no time, go quickly.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 없으니까 + 빨리 가요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The road is blocked, so stop.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no road-blocking mentioned</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q9',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Let's eat quickly.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ no eating mentioned</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">시간이 없<b class=\"hl\">으니까</b></span> = \"because there is no time\" → <b class=\"hl\">빨리 가요</b> (go quickly).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The reason (없으니까) and the action (빨리) fit option 2.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 없 ends in ㅆ → <b class=\"hl\">-으니까</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[18-10] Listening — 콘서트 가요</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct answer.</div>\n<button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('오늘 콘서트가 7시예요. 버스는 느리고 지하철은 빨라요. 그래서 지하철로 갑니다.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">Choose the best summary.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u18q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> He takes the subway to the 7 o'clock concert.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ fast subway → 7시 concert</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> He takes the slow bus.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 버스는 느려요 = the slow bus, rejected</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> The concert is at 6 o'clock.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 7시예요 = 7 o'clock</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u18q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> He walks to the concert.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 지하철로 = by subway, not walking</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u18q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Concert = 7시, bus = slow, subway = fast, and he takes the <b class=\"hl\">subway</b> → <b class=\"hl\">subway to a 7 o'clock concert</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The others mix up the time and the rejected bus.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for the decision word <span class=\"pt-ko\">그래서</span> = \"so / therefore\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>갑시다! — The Leader's Battle Cry</h3>\n    <p>Watch any K-POP behind-the-scenes video and you'll hear the leader shout <b>\"자, 갑시다!\"</b> to move the team from the waiting room to the stage. To keep fans safe coming out of a big concert, staff shout <b>\"여기로 가 주세요!\"</b> (Please go this way!) — everyone keeps calm and moves together.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ Next time you need to move a group, be the leader: point where you're going and say <b>\"지하철로 갑시다!\"</b> (let's take the subway!) or <b>\"빨리 서두릅시다!\"</b> (let's hurry!).</div>\n  </div>\n"}]}, {"id": 19, "title": "Come buy it with me", "en": "저랑 같이 사러 가요", "theme": "together", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 19 · SHOPPING TOGETHER</div>"}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">19</div><div><h2>Come buy it with me</h2><div class=\"en\">저랑 같이 사러 가요 — Shopping together · V-러 가다</div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · Together</span>\n      <h3>로이의 쇼핑 데이트 — \"저랑 같이 사러 가요!\"</h3>\n      <p>막내 <b>로이</b>는 시장에서 파는 <b>음식</b>이 정말 궁금해요. \"나 시장에 가고 싶어!\" 하고 외치자 <b>아란</b>이 웃으며 말해요. \"저랑 같이 <b>사러</b> 가요!\" — 두 사람은 함께 시장으로 달려가요. 🧺</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">The youngest member <b>Roy</b> is dying to try the <b>food</b> sold at the market. When he shouts \"I want to go!\" <b>Aran</b> smiles and says, \"Come buy (it) <b>with me</b>!\" — the two race to the market together. 🧺</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">🤝 GLOW POINT 획득 — Inviting a friend to go do something together!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🛍️</span> Invite a friend to go do something</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🎯</span> -러 가다 (go to do ~)</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🤝</span> 저랑 같이 & -고 싶어요 (want to)</div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 19 — Market Trip</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">🛒 At the market</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">시장에 뭐가 있어요? 저는 음식을 사고 싶어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">What is at the market? I want to buy food!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">알겠어요. 저랑 같이 사러 가요!</div><div class=\"gl\">Got it. Come buy (it) together with me!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">좋아요! 저는 떡볶이를 먹고 싶어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Great! I want to eat tteokbokki.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">여기 옷도 예뻐요. 같이 볼래요?</div><div class=\"gl\">The clothes here are pretty too. Want to look together?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">네! 저랑 같이 쇼핑해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Yes! Let's shop together with me.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-러 가다 — \"go (somewhere) to do ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add to a verb stem to say you go somewhere <b>in order to do</b> that action. After a vowel (사다→사) use <b>-러</b>; after a consonant (먹다→먹) use <b>-으러</b>. The going verb (가요 / 왔어요) comes at the end.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">사<b>러</b> 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">사다 (vowel) → 사러 · \"I go (somewhere) to buy.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">먹<b>으러</b> 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">먹다 (consonant) → 먹으러 · \"I go to eat.\"</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">시장에 뭐 사러 가요?</span><span class=\"gl\">What do you go to the market to buy?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">저랑 같이 / 함께 — \"together with (me)\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\"><b>저랑</b> = \"with me\" (저 + -랑). Place it before <b>같이</b> (= \"together\") to say \"together with me.\" After a vowel use -랑 (저랑), after a consonant use -이랑. <b>함께</b> is a slightly more formal twin of 같이.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">저<b>랑 같이</b> 사러 가요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Come buy (it) together with me.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">친구<b>랑 같이</b> 쇼핑해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">I shop together with a friend.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">팬들과 <b>함께</b> 노래해요.</span><span class=\"gl\">We sing together with the fans.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-고 싶어요 — \"I want to ~\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>-고 싶어요</b> to a verb stem to say what you <b>want to do</b>. It works on every verb — no consonant/vowel change needed. Raise the tone to ask \"Do you want to…?\"</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">떡볶이를 먹<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to eat tteokbokki.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">옷을 사<b>고 싶어요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">I want to buy clothes.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">같이 가<b>고 싶어요</b>?</span><span class=\"gl\">Do you want to go together?</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"저랑 같이 사러 가요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">저랑 같이 사러 가요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"Come buy (it) together with me.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">This is the sentence you say before a fun trip with fans or friends. Why does <b>러</b> appear — and what is <b>저랑</b> doing at the front?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      English says \"let's go buy it.\" Korean says the same idea in a different order: the <b>action</b> you want to do comes first — <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> \"to buy\" — then the verb for <b>going</b>, <span class=\"pt-ko\">가요</span>. The little <span class=\"pt-ko\">러</span> glued onto 사 is the bridge that means <b>\"in order to\"</b>: 사(다) → 사<b>러</b> = \"in order to buy.\" So the sentence reads literally: with-me together, in-order-to-buy go.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">저<b>랑</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">with me <span class=\"t-sub\">(companion)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">저 = humble \"I.\" Add <b>-랑</b> to mean \"with.\" 저 ends in a vowel → 저랑.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">같이</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">together <span class=\"t-sub\">(adverb)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">같이 doubles up with 저랑 for warmth. 함께 is its more formal twin — think stage speeches.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">사러 가요</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">go (to) buy <span class=\"t-sub\">(V-러 가다)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">사다 stem 사 + <b>-러</b> + 가요. 먹다 → 먹<b>으러</b> 가요.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">V-러 가다 = \"go to do ~\"</b> — say the ACTION (사러) first, then GOING (가요). One bridge particle <span class=\"pt-ko\">러</span> does all the work.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Vowel stem → -러</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">사<b>러</b> 가요 · 보<b>러</b> 가요</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">사다·보다 → \"go to buy / go to see\"</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Consonant stem → -으러</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">먹<b>으러</b> 가요 · 잡<b>으러</b> 가요</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">먹다·잡다 → \"go to eat / go to catch\"</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> want something? Use <span class=\"pt-ko\">-고 싶어요</span> (\"I want to\"). Going to do it? Use <span class=\"pt-ko\">-러 가요</span>. Bringing a friend along? Lead with <span class=\"pt-ko\">저랑 같이</span>. Combine them: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저랑 같이 먹으러 가고 싶어요.</span>\n  </div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🛍️</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">쇼핑과 장소<small>Shopping · 사다/가다/쇼핑/시장</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b19_money.webp\" alt=\"사다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('사다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">사다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to buy</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b19_go.webp\" alt=\"가다\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가다')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가다</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gada</div><div class=\"vw-en\">to go</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_shopping.webp\" alt=\"쇼핑\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('쇼핑')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">쇼핑</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">syoping</div><div class=\"vw-en\">shopping</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u8_market.webp\" alt=\"시장\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시장')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">시장</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">sijang</div><div class=\"vw-en\">market</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('시장에 뭐 사러 가요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">시장에 뭐 사러 가요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">What do you go to the market to buy?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이 쇼핑할까요?')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">같이 쇼핑할까요?</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Shall we shop together?</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식을 사러 가요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">음식을 사러 가요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I go to buy food.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🛍️ <b>같이 쓰는 말:</b> 사다 + 쇼핑 + 시장 = heading to the <b>market</b> to <b>buy</b>. \"Go buy\" is <span class=\"pt-ko\">사러 가요</span> — V-러 가다!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🧺</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">물건과 함께<small>Things · 옷/음식/함께/같이</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b12_tshirt.webp\" alt=\"옷\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('옷')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">옷</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">ot</div><div class=\"vw-en\">clothes</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/u5_food.webp\" alt=\"음식\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('음식')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">음식</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eumsik</div><div class=\"vw-en\">food</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_together.webp\" alt=\"함께\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('함께')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">함께</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hamkke</div><div class=\"vw-en\">together (formal)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b10_together.webp\" alt=\"같이\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('같이')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">같이</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gachi</div><div class=\"vw-en\">together (casual)</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('이 옷이 예뻐요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">이 옷이 예뻐요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">These clothes are pretty.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저랑 같이 사러 가요!')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저랑 같이 사러 가요!</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Come buy (it) together with me!</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('팬들과 함께 노래해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">팬들과 함께 노래해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">We sing together with the fans.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🧺 <b>주의:</b> <b>함께</b> feels more formal (speeches, songs); <b>같이</b> is everyday talk. Both mean \"together\"!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-1] Reading — Fill in the blank (V-러 가다)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">시장에 음식을 <b>＿＿</b> 가요. (I go to the market to buy food.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 사러<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 사(다)+러 가요 = \"in order to buy\" — 사 ends in a vowel → 사러</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 사고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 사고 = \"buy and…\" (connects actions), not \"go to buy\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 사서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 사서 = \"because I buy / buy and then\" (reason), not movement</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 사면<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 사면 = \"if I buy\" (condition)</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The <span class=\"pt-ko\">사다</span> stem ends in the vowel <b class=\"hl\">ㅏ</b>, so we attach <span class=\"pt-ko\">-러</span> (not -으러): <span class=\"pt-ko\">사러 가요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">사고</b> connects verbs (buy-and), <b class=\"hl\">사서</b> gives a reason (buy-so), <b class=\"hl\">사면</b> is a condition (if-buy). Only <b class=\"hl\">-러 가다</b> means \"go in order to do.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-2] Reading — Meaning of -러 가다</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the closest meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">로이는 시장에 <b>사러</b> 갔어요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Roy went to the market and bought food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ He went <b>to buy</b> — we don't know yet what he bought</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Roy went to the market in order to buy something.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ -러 가다 = \"go in order to do\" → went to buy</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Roy bought a ticket to go to the market.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 사러 refers to the market items, not a ticket</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q2',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Roy came from the market after buying.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 갔어요 means <b>went</b>, not came</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The pattern <span class=\"pt-ko\">V-러 가다</span> stresses the <b class=\"hl\">purpose of going</b>: 사러 = \"in order to buy.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The action isn't finished, so we cannot say he \"bought food\" already.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">LISTENING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-3] Listening — What does Roy want to do?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what Roy wants to do.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">로이: \"저는 음식을 사고 싶어요.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Roy wants to sing a song.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ He says nothing about singing</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Roy wants to sleep.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not what he says</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Roy wants to go home.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ He wants to shop, not leave</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q3',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> Roy wants to buy food.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 사고 싶어요 = \"I want to buy\" → food</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">In <span class=\"pt-ko\">음식을 사고 싶어요</span>, the object is <b class=\"hl\">음식</b> (food) and the verb is <span class=\"pt-ko\">사고 싶어요</span> = \"want to buy.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">-고 싶어요</b> always means \"want to <verb>\" — whatever noun is before it is what is wanted.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-4] Reading — 저랑 같이</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct phrase for \"together with me.\"</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\"><b>＿＿</b> 같이 사러 가요!</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 친구랑<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 친구랑 = \"with a friend\", not \"with me\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 팬들이랑<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 팬들이랑 = \"with the fans\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저랑<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 저(me) + 랑(with) = \"together with me\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q4',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 누구랑<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 누구랑 = \"with whom?\" (a question)</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To say \"together <b class=\"hl\">with me</b>\" use <span class=\"pt-ko\">저랑 같이</span>. <b class=\"hl\">저랑</b> = 저 (humble I) + -랑 (with).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 친구랑/팬들이랑 both mean \"with someone else,\" not \"with me.\"</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">LISTENING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-5] Listening — Choose what you hear</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the correct sentence you hear.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 (음성: 저랑 같이 사러 가요)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 저는 같이 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ You hear 저랑 (with me), not 저는</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저랑 같이 사러 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ Matches the audio exactly</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 저랑 같이 먹어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ The verb is 사러 (to buy), not 먹어요 (eat)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q5',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 혼자 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ You hear 같이 (together), not 혼자 (alone)</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Listen for the key pieces: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저랑</span> (with me) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">같이</span> (together) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">사러 가요</span> (go to buy).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Focus on the <b class=\"hl\">ending verb</b> — 사러 가요 vs 먹어요 changes the whole meaning.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-6] Reading — 함 vs -으러 받침</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct form after a consonant stem.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">아란은 떡볶이를 <b>＿＿</b> 가요. (Aran goes to eat tteokbokki.)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 먹으러<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 먹다 ends in ㄱ (consonant) → 먹으러 가요</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 먹러<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ A consonant stem needs -으러, not -러</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 먹고<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 먹고 가요 would mean \"eats and goes,\" not \"goes to eat\"</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 먹어서<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 먹어서 = \"because (she) eats,\" a reason</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">A stem ending in a <b class=\"hl\">consonant</b> (먹) takes <span class=\"pt-ko\">-으러</span>: <span class=\"pt-ko\">먹으러 가요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Same rule as everything else in Korean: consonant → add 으; vowel → no 으. Compare 사다(ㅏ) → 사<b class=\"hl\">러</b> vs 먹다(ㄱ) → 먹<b class=\"hl\">으러</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-7] Reading — Vocab: where do you buy food?</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the best place.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">음식을 사려면 어디에 가요? (Where do you go to buy food?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 연습실<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 연습실 = practice room (for dancing/singing)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 시장<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 시장 = market — the place you go to buy food and things</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 무대<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 무대 = stage (for performing)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q7',1,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 기숙사<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 기숙사 = dormitory</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The natural place to <b class=\"hl\">buy food</b> (음식을 사다) is the <span class=\"pt-ko\">시장</span> (market).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 연습실/무대 are where an idol <b>practices/ performs</b>, not where you shop for food.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">LISTENING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-8] Listening — Best reply</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best reply.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">아란: \"같이 쇼핑할까요?\" (Shall we shop together?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 아니요, 저는 혼자예요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Roy is excited, not refusing</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 저는 노래를 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Off-topic — doesn't answer the invitation</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 시장이 어디예요?<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Asking where a market is isn't the natural answer</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q8',3,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 네, 저랑 같이 가요!<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ \"Yes, come with me!\" — agrees and invites back</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">To a friendly suggestion (<span class=\"pt-ko\">같이 쇼핑할까요?</span>), the natural answer agrees and keeps the together tone: <span class=\"pt-ko\">저랑 같이 가요!</span></div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 \"together\" language flows both ways — reply with 같이/저랑 to keep the invitation warm.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">READING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-9] Reading — Meaning of a sentence</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the closest meaning.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">팬들과 <b>함께</b> 음식을 사러 가요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> I buy food alone.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 함께 means together, not alone</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> The fans go alone to buy food.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ 함께 팬들과 = with the fans, not alone</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> (We) go with the fans to buy food together.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 함께 = together · 사러 가요 = go to buy</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q9',2,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> I practice singing with the fans.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ The verb is 사다 (buy), not practice</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\"><span class=\"pt-ko\">팬들과 함께</span> = \"together with the fans,\" and <span class=\"pt-ko\">음식을 사러 가요</span> = \"go to buy food.\"</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 <b class=\"hl\">함께</b> is the more formal \"together\" — you often hear idols use it in fan-meeting greetings.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">LISTENING</span><span class=\"p-title\">[19-10] Listening — Choose the picture</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the picture that matches.</div>\n  <div class=\"p-q\">🔊 (음성: 시장에서 옷을 사고 싶어요)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u19q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 🛒👗 (a market with clothes)<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ ✅ 시장(market) + 옷(clothes) + 사고 싶어요(want to buy)</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 🎤🎵 (a stage with a microphone)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not about a stage or singing</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 🍽️🏠 (food at home)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ It's clothes at a market, not food at home</span></button><button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u19q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 💼🚶 (an office with a person walking)<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ ❌ Not about an office</span></button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u19q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Break the sentence into images: <span class=\"pt-ko\">시장</span> (market) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">옷</span> (clothes) + <span class=\"pt-ko\">사고 싶어요</span> (want to buy).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listening with pictures = pick the one that matches <b>place + object + verb</b>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Going Together — Fan Meet Invites</h3>\n    <p>Idols love doing things <b>together with fans</b>. Whether it's a food truck, a market snack run, or buying <b>음식</b> after a show, the invite always leads with togetherness.</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">✍️ \"저랑 같이 ○○하러 가요!\" — Fill in your verb (사러/먹으러/보러) and invite a friend to go do it with you!</div>\n  </div>"}]}, {"id": 20, "title": "My mother likes flowers", "en": "어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요", "theme": "honorifics", "sections": [{"cls": "unit-flag", "html": "<div class=\"unit-flag\">UNIT 20 · HONORIFICS &amp; FAMILY</div>\n  "}, {"cls": "sec-title", "html": "<div class=\"sec-title\"><div class=\"no\">20</div><div><h2>My Mother Likes Flowers</h2><div class=\"en\">어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요 — Honorifics &amp; family</div></div></div>\n  "}, {"cls": "story", "html": "<div class=\"story\">\n    <img class=\"story-art\" src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n    <div class=\"story-body\">\n      <span class=\"story-tag\">💿 GLOWSIS STORY · 20/20</span>\n      <h3>채아의 가족 이야기 — \"어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요\"</h3>\n      <p>데부 후 처음으로 집에 간 <b>채아</b>는 가족 사진을 팜들에게 보여 줘요. 어머니께서는 꽃을 좋아하세요. 채아는 형/누나/언니/오빠 같이 가족을 부르는 법도 가르침 준다다. 🌷</p>\n      <p class=\"story-en\">After debut, <b>Chaea</b> visits home for the first time and shows her family photos to the fans. Her <b>mother likes flowers</b>. Chaea also teaches how to call family — 형, 누나, 언니, 오빠. 🌷</p>\n      <span class=\"story-piece\">💛 GLOW POINT 20/20 획득 — Honorifics &amp; family!</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n"}, {"cls": "goals", "html": "<div class=\"goals\">\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🗣️</span> Speak politely about elders</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">🙇</span> 께서 &amp; -시- honorifics</div>\n    <div class=\"goal\"><span class=\"g-ico\">👨‍👩‍👧</span> Family vocabulary</div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "dialog", "html": "<div class=\"dialog\">\n    <div class=\"d-head\">\n      <span class=\"d-title\">💬 Dialogue 20 — Talking About Family</span>\n      <span class=\"d-scene\">📺 Backstage, after a show</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">채아야, 주말에 뭐 했어?</div><div class=\"gl\">Chaea, what did you do on the weekend?</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/chaea.webp\" alt=\"채아\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">채아</div><div class=\"ko\">집에 갔어요. 어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요. 그래서 꽃을 사 드렸어요.</div><div class=\"gl\">I went home. My mother likes flowers, so I bought her some.</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/roy.webp\" alt=\"로이\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">로이</div><div class=\"ko\">우리 아버지께서는 회사원이세요. 참 열심히 일하세요!</div><div class=\"gl\">My father is an office worker. He works so hard!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line me\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/dahee.webp\" alt=\"다희\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">다희</div><div class=\"ko\">할머니께서는 김치를 정말 잘 만드세요. 형하고 오빠가 다 먹어요!</div><div class=\"gl\">My grandmother makes kimchi really well. My older brothers eat it all up!</div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"d-line\"><img src=\"assets/glowsis/aran.webp\" alt=\"아란\">\n      <div class=\"d-bubble\"><div class=\"who\">아란</div><div class=\"ko\">가족 이야기를 들으니까 마음이 따뜻해요.</div><div class=\"gl\">Hearing about family warms my heart.</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 1</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">께서 — Formal subject honorific</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Add <b>께서</b> after a person you respect (parents, grandparents, teachers) INSTEAD of 이/가. It politely marks WHO is doing the action.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어머니<b>께서</b> 꽃을 좋아하세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Mother (honored) likes flowers.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아버지<b>께서</b> 신문을 읽으세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Father (honored) reads the newspaper.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">할아버지<b>께서</b> 차를 드세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Grandfather (honored) drinks tea.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 2</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">-시- — Honorific suffix in the verb</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Slipped into a verb, <b>-시-</b> honors the SUBJECT (who does it). It pairs perfectly with 께서. Stems ending in a vowel take <b>-시-</b>; stems ending in a consonant take <b>-으시-</b>.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">좋아하<b>시</b>다 → 좋아하세요</span><span class=\"gl\">Ending ㅏ (vowel) → -시-</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">읽<b>으시</b>다 → 읽으세요</span><span class=\"gl\">Ending ㄱ (consonant) → -으시-</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">할머니께서 주무세요.</span><span class=\"gl\">Grandma is sleeping (주무시다 = sleeping of elders).</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "grammar", "html": "<div class=\"grammar\">\n    <span class=\"g-label\">GRAMMAR 3</span>\n    <div class=\"g-point\">어머니께서 …하세요 — The full polite pattern</div>\n    <div class=\"g-rule\">Put 께서 (honor the person) and -세요 (honor the action) together. It becomes a calm, respectful way to talk about what an older person does. Perfect for showing love toward family.</div>\n    <div class=\"g-ex\">\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">어머니<b>께서</b> 꽃을 좋아하<b>세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Mother likes flowers.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">아버지<b>께서</b> 회사에 가<b>세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Father goes to work.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ex\"><span class=\"ko\">할머니<b>께서</b> 노래를 부르<b>세요</b>.</span><span class=\"gl\">Grandmother sings.</span></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n"}, {"cls": "teach", "html": "<div class=\"teach\">\n  <span class=\"t-label\">🧑🏻‍🏫 Teacher's Deep-Dive · Breaking down \"어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요\"</span>\n  <div class=\"t-q\"><span class=\"t-ko\">어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요.</span> <span class=\"t-en\">= \"My mother (honorably) likes flowers.\"</span></div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-row t-head\">\n    <div class=\"t-why\">Why does Korean \"raise\" the mother with <b>께서</b> and <b>-세요</b>?</div>\n    <div class=\"t-deep\">\n      Korean marks <b>respect inside the sentence</b>. When the person doing the action is someone you honor — an <b>older family\n      member</b> or a <b>teacher</b> — the subject marker 이/가 changes to <span class=\"pt-ko\">께서</span>, and the verb grows an\n      honorific <span class=\"pt-ko\">-시-</span> inside it. So \"Mother likes flowers\" becomes\n      <b>어머니<b>께서</b> 꽃을 좋아하<b>세요</b></b>. Same meaning — but it politely lifts the mother up.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-grid\">\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">어머니<b>께서</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">mother <span class=\"t-sub\">(honored subject)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">께서 replaces 이/가 for respected people. You almost never say 어머니<b>가</b> when politely describing her.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">꽃을</div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">flowers <span class=\"t-sub\">(object)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">꽃 ends in a consonant (철) → object particle <b>을</b>.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"t-op\">+</div>\n    <div class=\"t-cell t-eqcell\">\n      <div class=\"t-word\">좋아하<b>세요</b></div>\n      <div class=\"t-role\">likes <span class=\"t-sub\">(-시- + 어요)</span></div>\n      <div class=\"t-note\">좋아하<b>시</b> + 어요 → 좋아하<b>세요</b>. The -시- is what \"raises\" the mother.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-insight\">\n    <b class=\"t-i-ko\">께서 + -시- = one polite \"package\".</b> You can use either alone, but together they sound natural and warm —\n    like saying \"my dear mother (whom I respect)\". It's how K-POP idols proudly describe their parents on camera.\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-compare\">\n    <div class=\"t-c-a\"><b>Everyday (to friends)</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어머니<b>가</b> 꽃을 좋아<b>해요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Plain 이/가 + 해요.</span></div>\n    <div class=\"t-c-b\"><b>Polite / respectful</b><br><span class=\"t-ko\">어머니<b>께서</b> 꽃을 좋아하<b>세요</b>.</span><br><span class=\"t-en\">Honored 께서 + 하세요.</span></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"t-tip\">\n    💡 <b>Memory tip:</b> think of 께서 as the \"bow\" and -시- as the \"lift\". When an elder is the subject, <b>bow (께서)</b>\n    and then <b>lift the verb (-세요)</b>. Same for any respected person: <span class=\"pt-ko\">선생님께서 가르치세요</span> = \"The teacher teaches.\"\n  </div>\n</div>\n"}, {"cls": "vocab-lab", "html": "<div class=\"vocab-lab\"><div class=\"vl-toolbar\"><span class=\"vl-hint\">카테고리를 눌러 그림과 함께 공부하세요</span><button class=\"vl-expand\" onclick=\"glowVocabAll()\">모두 펼치기</button></div><div class=\"vl-cat open\" data-tone=\"pink\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">🌷</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">부모님<small>Parents · 어머니 &amp; 아버지</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_mother.webp\" alt=\"어머니\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어머니')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">어머니</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eomeoni</div><div class=\"vw-en\">mother</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_father.webp\" alt=\"아버지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아버지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">아버지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">abeoji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">father</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어머니께서 꽃을 좋아하세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Mother likes flowers.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('아버지께서 신문을 읽으세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">아버지께서 신문을 읽으세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Father reads the newspaper.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('어머니께서 음식을 만드세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">어머니께서 음식을 만드세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Mother cooks.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">🌷 <b>함께 쓰는 말:</b> 부모님을 말할 때 <b>께서 …-세요</b>로 높여요. Polite \"mother/father\" always come with respect.</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"sky\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👵</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">조부모님<small>Grandparents · 할머니 &amp; 할아버지</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">2</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_grandma.webp\" alt=\"할머니\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('할머니')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">할머니</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">halmeoni</div><div class=\"vw-en\">grandmother</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_grandpa.webp\" alt=\"할아버지\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('할아버지')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">할아버지</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">harabeoji</div><div class=\"vw-en\">grandfather</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('할머니께서 김치를 만드세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">할머니께서 김치를 만드세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Grandmother makes kimchi.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('할아버지께서 산책을 하세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">할아버지께서 산책을 하세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Grandfather takes a walk.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('할머니께서 손자를 사랑하세요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">할머니께서 손자를 사랑하세요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Grandmother loves her grandchildren.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👵 <b>조부모님:</b> 할머니 = grandmother, 할아버지 = grandfather. They are the most honored people — always 께서 …-세요!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"lav\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">💘</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">형제자매<small>Older siblings · 형·오빠·누나·언니</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">4</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_man.webp\" alt=\"형\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('형')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">형</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">hyeong</div><div class=\"vw-en\">older brother (a boy says)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_man.webp\" alt=\"오빠\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오빠')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">오빠</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">oppa</div><div class=\"vw-en\">older brother (a girl says)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_woman.webp\" alt=\"누나\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('누나')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">누나</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">nuna</div><div class=\"vw-en\">older sister (a boy says)</div></div></div><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_woman.webp\" alt=\"언니\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('언니')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">언니</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">eonni</div><div class=\"vw-en\">older sister (a girl says)</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('형이 운동을 해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">형이 운동을 해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(My) older brother exercises. (a boy speaking)</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('오빠가 선물을 줌어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">오빠가 선물을 줌어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(My) older brother gave me a gift. (a girl speaking)</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('누나가 노래를 잘해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">누나가 노래를 잘해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(My) older sister sings well. (a boy speaking)</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('언니가 옹을 사 줌어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">언니가 옹을 사 줌어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">(My) older sister bought me clothes. (a girl speaking)</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">💘 <b>같은 뜻, 다른 말:</b> the word for your older sibling depends on YOUR gender. Girl→오빠/언니, Boy→형/누나. On stage, fans use the same words for idols!</div></div></div><div class=\"vl-cat\" data-tone=\"mint\"><button class=\"vl-cat-head\" onclick=\"glowVocab(this)\"><span class=\"vl-cat-ico\">👨‍👩‍👧</span><span class=\"vl-cat-name\">우리 가족<small>Family · 사랑하는 사람들</small></span><span class=\"vl-cat-count\">1</span><span class=\"vl-cat-arr\">▾</span></button><div class=\"vl-cat-body\"><div class=\"vw-grid\"><div class=\"vw-card\"><div class=\"vw-pic\"><img src=\"assets/vocab/1b20_family.webp\" alt=\"가족\"></div><div class=\"vw-info\"><button class=\"vw-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가족')\">🔊</button><div class=\"vw-ko\">가족</div><div class=\"vw-rom\">gajok</div><div class=\"vw-en\">family</div></div></div></div><div class=\"vs-box\"><div class=\"vs-head\">💬 자주 쓰는 말 · Phrases you'll hear a lot</div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('저는 가족을 사랑해요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">저는 가족을 사랑해요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I love my family.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('우리 가족은 네 명이에요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">우리 가족은 네 명이에요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">Our family has four people.</span></div></div><div class=\"vs-line\"><button class=\"vs-tts\" onclick=\"tts('가족하고 같이 저녁을 먹어요.')\">🔊</button><div><span class=\"vs-ko\">가족하고 같이 저녁을 먹어요.</span> <span class=\"vs-en\">I have dinner with my family.</span></div></div></div><div class=\"vl-link\">👨‍👩‍👧 <b>가족 = family.</b> All of today's words are your 가족 — gather them all: 가족을 사랑해요!</div></div></div></div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-1 Reading — 께서 (honorific subject)]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correct honorific subject marker.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">어머니(　) 꽃을 좋아하세요.</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q1\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 께서<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 께서 politely marks Mother as the honored subject</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 가<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 가 is plain and doesn't honor the mother</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 은<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 은 is a topic marker, not a subject honorific</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q1',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 를<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 를 marks the object, not the subject</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q1\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The honored subject marker <b class=\"hl\">께서</b> replaces <span class=\"pt-ko\">이/가</span> for respected people.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">가</b> doesn't honor; <b class=\"hl\">은</b> marks topic and <b class=\"hl\">를</b> marks the object.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Family + 께서 = polite. 어머니<b>께서</b> is the respectful way to say \"mother (does…)\".</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-2 Reading — -시- vs -으시-]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Choose the correctly honored verb.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">Which one is the polite -시- form of 읽다 (to read)?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q2\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 읽으세요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 읽다 ends in consonant ㄱ → 읽으시- + 어요</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 읽세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Missing the -으- that follows a consonant</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 좋아하세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ That's the honored form of 좋아하다, not 읽다</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q2',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 읽어요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ This has no honorific -시- at all</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q2\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">Verb stems ending in a <b class=\"hl\">consonant</b> take <span class=\"pt-ko\">-으시-</span>, so <span class=\"pt-ko\">읽다</span> (ㄱ) → <span class=\"pt-ko\">읽으세요</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Stems ending in a <b class=\"hl\">vowel</b> take just <span class=\"pt-ko\">-시-</span> (좋아하다 → 좋아하<b>세</b>요).</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 After a 받침 use -으시-, after a vowel use -시-.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-3 Reading — 어머니께서 …하세요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Which sentence talks about Mother MOST politely?</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">다음 중 가장 정중한 문장은? (Which is the most polite sentence?)</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q3\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 어머니께서 음식을 만드세요.<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 께서 honors Mother + -세요 honors the verb</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어머니가 음식을 만들어요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Plain 이/가 and no -시-</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 아버지가 회사에 가요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ About the father and not polite</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q3',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 저는 꽃을 좋아해요.<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ About the speaker (저), not the mother</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q3\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The most polite sentence uses <b class=\"hl\">께서</b> AND <b class=\"hl\">-세요</b> together — the full respectful package.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The plain sentence (이/가 + 만들어요) isn't raised, and the others talk about the wrong person.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 To speak warmly about an elder: <span class=\"pt-ko\">[family]께서 …-[세요]</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-4 Reading — 할머니께서 노래하세요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose WHO sings.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">\"할머니께서는 노래를 잘 부르세요. 할아버지께서는 운동을 좋아하세요.\" — 누가 노래를 잘 부르세요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q4\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 할머니<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ Grandmother sings well (노래를 잘 부르세요)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 할아버지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Grandfather likes exercise, not singing</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 어머니<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Mother is not mentioned</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q4',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 아버지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Father is not mentioned</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q4\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The passage says <span class=\"pt-ko\">할머니께서는 노래를 잘 부르세요</span> — the grandmother sings well.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The grandfather likes <b class=\"hl\">exercise</b> (운동), not singing.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Listen for 께서 — it tells you WHO the honored subject is.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-5 Reading — 오빠 vs 형]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">A girl talks about her older brother. Which word does she use?</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">유나는 여자예요. 유나의 오빠가 선물을 줌었어요. — How does 유나 call her older brother?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q5\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 오빠<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ A girl calls her older brother 오빠</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 형<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 형 is used by a boy</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 누나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 누나 = older sister, said by a boy</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q5',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 언니<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 언니 = older sister, said by a girl</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q5\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The word for \"older brother\" depends on the speaker's <b class=\"hl\">gender</b>. A girl says <span class=\"pt-ko\">오빠</span>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">형</b> is only for a boy; <b class=\"hl\">누나/언니</b> are for older sisters.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Girl → 오빠 (brother), 언니 (sister). Boy → 형 (brother), 누나 (sister).</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-6 Reading — 아버지의 직업]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">Read and choose the father's job.</div>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">\"우리 아버지께서는 회사원이세요. 아주 열심히 일하세요.\" — 아버지께서는 무슨 일을 하세요?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q6\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 회사원이세요<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ The father is an office worker (회사원)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 의사세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No doctor here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 선생님이세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No teacher here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q6',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 가수세요<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No singer here</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q6\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The passage says <span class=\"pt-ko\">아버지께서는 회사원이세요</span> — the father is an <b class=\"hl\">office worker</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 의사/선생님/가수 are jobs not in the text.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Jobs of elders also get 께서 + -세요: <span class=\"pt-ko\">회사원이세요</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-7 Listening — 할머니의 김치]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose what the grandmother does well.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('할머니께서 김치를 정말 잘 만드세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">What does grandmother make well?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q7\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 김치<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ You heard 김치를 정말 잘 만드세요 = makes kimchi well</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 꽃<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 꽃 (flowers) was not said</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 옹<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 옹 (clothes) was not said</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q7',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 차<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 차 (tea) was not said</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q7\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The audio says <span class=\"pt-ko\">할머니께서 김치를 정말 잘 만드세요</span> — grandmother makes <b class=\"hl\">kimchi</b> well.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ 꽃/옹/차 are other words not in the clip.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Key noun = 김치, key verb = 만들다 (to make), raised with -세요.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-8 Listening — 누가 사랑하세요]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose WHO is honored.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('할머니께서 저를 정말 사랑하세요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">Who loves the speaker?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q8\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 할머니<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 할머니께서 …사랑하세요 = Grandmother loves me</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 어머니<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not the mother here</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 누나<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not the older sister</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q8',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 할아버지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not the grandfather</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q8\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">께서 names the <b class=\"hl\">honored subject</b> — here it's <span class=\"pt-ko\">할머니</span>, who <b class=\"hl\">loves</b> (사랑하세요) the speaker.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ The other family words were not said.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Grandmother = <span class=\"pt-ko\">할머니</span>, grandfather = <span class=\"pt-ko\">할아버지</span>.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-9 Listening — 누구의 선물]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose WHO gave the gift.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('오빠가 선물을 사 줌었어요. 저는 정말 기뼈어요!')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">A girl is talking. Who bought her the gift?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q9\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> 오빠<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 오빠 = her older brother (a girl's word)</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> 언니<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 언니 would be an older sister</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> 형<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ 형 is a boy's word</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q9',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> 아버지<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ Not the father</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q9\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The speaker says <span class=\"pt-ko\">오빠가 선물을 사 줌었어요</span> — because it's a <b class=\"hl\">girl</b> speaking, her older brother is <b class=\"hl\">오빠</b>.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ <b class=\"hl\">언니</b> is an older sister and <b class=\"hl\">형</b> belongs to a boy.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Same person, different word by the speaker's gender — that's Korean family lingo!</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "practice", "html": "<div class=\"practice\">\n  <div class=\"p-head\"><span class=\"p-badge\">TOPIK TYPE</span><span class=\"p-title\">[20-10 Listening — 가족 소개]</span></div>\n  <div class=\"p-dir\">🔊 Listen and choose the best summary.</div>\n  <button class=\"p-audio\" onclick=\"tts('우리 가족은 네 명이에요. 아버지, 어머니, 언니, 그리고 저예요.')\">🔊 Listen</button>\n    <div class=\"p-q\">Which is the best summary of the family?</div>\n  <div class=\"opts\" data-q=\"u20q10\">\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">1</span> Four people: father, mother, older sister, and me<span class=\"o-gl\">✅ 네 명 = four: 아버지·어머니·언니·저</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">2</span> Five people with two older sisters<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ There's only one 언니, total four</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">3</span> Father, mother and grandfather<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ No grandfather was said</span></button>\n      <button class=\"opt\" onclick=\"checkQ('u20q10',0,this)\"><span class=\"o-idx\">4</span> A family of three people<span class=\"o-gl\">❌ The family has four, not three</span></button>\n        </div>\n  <div class=\"p-feedback\" id=\"fb-u20q10\"></div>\n  <div class=\"pt-note\"><div class=\"pt-note-head\">🧑🏻‍🏫 선생님 노트 · 문제 해설</div><div class=\"pt-note-body\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">The clip says <span class=\"pt-ko\">우리 가족은 네 명이에요. 아버지, 어머니, 언니, 그리고 저예요</span> — <b class=\"hl\">four</b> people.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">ⓞ Two sisters and a grandfather are not in the clip; it's not three people.</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:5px;\">💡 Count family with <span class=\"pt-ko\">네 명</span> (four people) and list them with 가족 = family.</div></div></div>\n</div>"}, {"cls": "culture", "html": "<div class=\"culture\">\n    <span class=\"c-label\">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>\n    <h3>Speak About Your Family with Respect — Like an Idol!</h3>\n    <p>On variety shows, idols talk about their parents with <b>께서 …-세요</b> to show love and respect. Try it: \"우리 어머니께서 정말 예빠세요!\"</p>\n    <div class=\"c-tip\">🙋 Fan lingo: girls call male idols <b>오빠</b> and female idols <b>언니</b>; boys call male idols <b>형</b> and female idols <b>누나</b>. It's the SAME family words you learned today — idols are like a big family to their fans!</div>\n  </div>\n"}]}];
